{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"c20ffdd3831cb8075b79801e21e92089d6ea1a6ff77c93a01b1ed2029c65a0c1","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Since there's no Tailwind or base-ui in the project, I'll port this to plain CSS and React, dropping the unnecessary render/merge abstractions and vendoring it as its own component file like GradualBlur was. I'll keep the measured indicator logic simplified while preserving the API shape with aria-pressed and data-checked attributes, and now I'm thinking through the label design for the segmented control.\n\nRather than a pill shape, I want a rounded-rectangle container with icon+text labels like \"Grid\" and \"List\", styled with a glass effect, a subtle lighter indicator fill, and a height around 34px to match existing sizing. I should also check how other settings are persisted, like localStorage usage elsewhere in the app, so this fits the same pattern.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"No Tailwind or Base UI in the project, so I'll port it to plain React and CSS, keeping coss's measured sliding indicator. Next, checking how preferences are saved."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Cmc7LNwR2oJtDPrW9Qjkck","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && grep -n \"localStorage\" src/*.tsx src/lib/*.ts | head -20; grep -n 'useState<\"general\"\\|settingsTab, setSettingsTab\\|type SettingsTab' src/App.tsx; ls src/components/GradualBlur; grep -n \"settings-data-row\\b\\|\\.settings-data-row {\" src/App.css | head -3","description":"Find settings persistence patterns"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
