{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","id":"edcf0635-5f32-477d-8275-2691b5105060","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:55:19.111Z","version":"2.1.306","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"8c442afde0ad22524f38da9d321150af6e542ac1f85aeedee23e13234fc4e050","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"41648c2e-f800-4ac5-9b07-55e702ba0735","keep":275,"tail":["dbe5c522c062ec93616997589c5f988936741b7014423858ddea830e35badc6b","edde2216e6113d956b74855d6926431cee8b87f8919fd0db69cd67f10c891782","ed8e804dccaf4d96201872c3c484af5388cd4c88992079593a4a26f236371ce1"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",277,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"9503e3283eec7b6c3b156e1bcde7e3ba01cf913799d8cbc813644060d4d1b196"}
{"parentUuid":"ff2f4aff-0f87-4274-886f-3128524d198b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFjV5NF71hiPhXMWr2wz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The kloq MIT version implements a segmented-control recipe as a radio group without the sliding indicator, using base-ui's RadioGroup. Since the sliding indicator in packages/ui is AGPL-licensed, I need to avoid copying that code and instead write my own version of the sliding indicator from scratch.\n\nI'll build the control using native radio inputs hidden inside labels — this gives accessible arrow-key navigation for free. For the sliding indicator, I'll measure the checked item's offset and width in a layout effect and animate its position with CSS transitions, since the label widths differ.\n\nI'll place this in SegmentedControl.tsx with a header crediting the kloq MIT recipe, plus a copy of the MIT license file for proper attribution since I'm adapting the structure and styling. I also want a small appearance settings module that stores the user's view toggle preference (pill vs segmented control) via a simple hook backed by localStorage.\n\nFor the settings UI, I'll dogfood the new SegmentedControl itself to let users pick between appearance options rather than reaching for a select element — it's a good fit since there are only two choices. The dock's segmented control will get the glass class so the liquid-glass treatment applies automatically, with an inner fill using the active glass variable, and each option will show an icon plus label like \"Grid\" and \"List\" to match the existing style conventions.\n\nI'm setting the indicator's checked state to track viewSelectionListMode directly, and tuning the shape — container radius 12px, items 9px, height 34px, padding 3px — to feel distinct from but consistent with the coss reference proportions. Now I need to extend the settings tab union to include an \"appearance\" entry and find a suitable icon, checking whether PaintBoardIcon exists in the hugeicons package for the tab button.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2328,"cache_read_input_tokens":214435,"output_tokens":1406,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1128},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2328,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1406,"cache_read_input_tokens":214435,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2328,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2328},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":16600,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFjV51B2kffY6nzDmwtQ","requestRef":"edcf0635-5f32-477d-8275-2691b5105060","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d7966952-a481-492c-95f5-2ce31ebae8b8","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:55:36.590Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
