{"parentUuid":"784a068c-1361-4baa-b6c4-b3541a5888d7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01XWrDvBB2ctE4377BFUnFnL","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"eaafda7d-bd90-4a3e-b042-bbf74a1487db","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:56:14.848Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"eaafda7d-bd90-4a3e-b042-bbf74a1487db","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFjWhdr2TkCWX696AFEN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm picking the first matching ref from the ls-remote output and building a generic string-value component styled after the coss segmented-control pattern.\n\nBuilding the SegmentedControl component...\n\nI'm checking that the indicator's position transition only kicks in after the first measured render, since the hidden state prevents any visible jump on mount, and since display:none elements don't animate transitions. I'm also noting that the visually-hidden radio needs a focus-visible outline on the parent label, using a `:has()` selector for accessibility.\n\nNow I'm resetting the fieldset's default border, padding, and sizing, then styling the segmented control container with flex layout, small gaps, rounded corners, and padding, while being careful that the glass background override from the global stylesheet doesn't get fought by CSS load order against my component styles.\n\nWriting item styles...\n\nStill writing indicator styles... I'm also checking the stacking context and offsetParent math so the indicator positions correctly relative to the fieldset, and confirming the dock height matches between pill and segmented variants before moving into the appearance module.\n\nNow I'm setting up the appearance config file that defines experimental UI variants toggled from Settings, starting with a view-toggle option between pill and segmented styles, then simplifying the typing by deriving the appearance type from the style constants directly.\n\nStill writing the hook logic...\n\nActually, I'm thinking about making this more scalable by generalizing validation into an options table keyed by each appearance property, so future settings get the same treatment automatically.\n\nI'm sketching the Settings Appearance panel with a header note about choices staying local, plus a row for the grid/list toggle using a segmented control with Pill/Segmented options. Then I move to wiring up App.tsx: importing the segmented control, the appearance hook, and options, and conditionally rendering the dock toggle based on the stored preference.\n\nI also need to add \"appearance\" to the settings tab union and insert its button after General, decide this stays out of user-facing docs since it's an experimental feature (just a changelog note under Added), and then write out the actual files.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":321,"cache_read_input_tokens":218286,"output_tokens":6126,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3567},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":321,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6126,"cache_read_input_tokens":218286,"cache_creation_input_tokens":321,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":321},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":32879,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFjWhJG6YYmzEtb8jEvy","requestRef":"165f20ed-dd30-4582-89af-3ddd462c7380","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"be59144e-8f06-4d8c-bb93-b3194c093e88","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:56:14.848Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"be59144e-8f06-4d8c-bb93-b3194c093e88","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFjWhdr2TkCWX696AFEN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L8UCFyf8GkF2eU2Q9Dxh7k","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > src/components/SegmentedControl/SegmentedControl.tsx <<'EOF'\n// The coss ui segmented-control recipe, as published MIT in cosscom/coss\n// packages/kloq @ 4339a256d21a3380745ba054f532e0ec5779930f\n// (src/lib/segmented-control.ts). Copyright (c) 2026 Sean Brydon; see LICENSE.md\n// in this directory. Rebuilt on native radios and plain CSS instead of Base UI\n// and Tailwind. The sliding indicator is inkling's own: the one in coss's\n// packages/ui is AGPL.\n\nimport { type ReactNode, useLayoutEffect, useRef, useState } from \"react\";\nimport \"./SegmentedControl.css\";\n\nexport type SegmentedControlOption<Value extends string> = {\n  value: Value;\n  label: string;\n  icon?: ReactNode;\n};\n\nexport function SegmentedControl<Value extends string>({\n  name,\n  label,\n  options,\n  value,\n  onChange,\n  className,\n}: {\n  /** Groups the radios, so it must be unique on the page. */\n  name: string;\n  /** Read by screen readers; not shown. */\n  label: string;\n  options: readonly SegmentedControlOption<Value>[];\n  value: Value;\n  onChange: (value: Value) => void;\n  className?: string;\n}) {\n  const rootRef = useRef<HTMLFieldSetElement>(null);\n  const [indicator, setIndicator] = useState<{ left: number; width: number } | null>(null);\n\n  useLayoutEffect(() => {\n    const root = rootRef.current;\n    if (!root) return;\n    const measure = () => {\n      const item = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-value=\"${CSS.escape(value)}\"]`);\n      setIndicator(item ? { left: item.offsetLeft, width: item.offsetWidth } : null);\n    };\n    measure();\n    const observer = new ResizeObserver(measure);\n    observer.observe(root);\n    return () => observer.disconnect();\n  }, [value]);\n\n  return (\n    <fieldset ref={rootRef} className={`segmented-control${className ? ` ${className}` : \"\"}`}>\n      <legend className=\"visually-hidden\">{label}</legend>\n      <span\n        className=\"segmented-control-indicator\"\n        aria-hidden=\"true\"\n        hidden={!indicator}\n        style={{ translate: `${indicator?.left ?? 0}px 0`, width: indicator?.width }}\n      />\n      {options.map((option) => (\n        <label\n          key={option.value}\n          className=\"segmented-control-item\"\n          data-value={option.value}\n          data-checked={option.value === value || undefined}\n        >\n          <input\n            type=\"radio\"\n            className=\"visually-hidden\"\n            name={name}\n            value={option.value}\n            checked={option.value === value}\n            onChange={() => onChange(option.value)}\n          />\n          {option.icon}\n          <span>{option.label}</span>\n        </label>\n      ))}\n    </fieldset>\n  );\n}\nEOF\ncat > src/components/SegmentedControl/SegmentedControl.css <<'EOF'\n/* No background of its own: callers add `.glass` or a surface. */\n.segmented-control {\n  position: relative;\n  z-index: 0;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 2px;\n  min-width: 0;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 3px;\n  border: 0;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n}\n.segmented-control-item {\n  position: relative;\n  display: inline-flex;\n  flex: 0 0 auto;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  gap: 6px;\n  height: 28px;\n  padding: 0 11px 0 9px;\n  border-radius: 9px;\n  color: var(--library-muted);\n  cursor: pointer;\n  font: 500 13px / 16px var(--font-ui);\n  white-space: nowrap;\n  user-select: none;\n  transition: color 0.15s ease;\n}\n.segmented-control-item:hover {\n  color: var(--library-text-soft);\n}\n.segmented-control-item[data-checked] {\n  color: var(--library-text);\n}\n.segmented-control-item svg {\n  display: block;\n  flex: 0 0 auto;\n  opacity: 0.8;\n}\n.segmented-control-item[data-checked] svg {\n  opacity: 1;\n}\n.segmented-control-item:has(input:focus-visible) {\n  outline: 2px solid var(--orange);\n  outline-offset: 1px;\n}\n.segmented-control-indicator {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: 3px;\n  bottom: 3px;\n  left: 0;\n  z-index: -1;\n  border-radius: 9px;\n  background: var(--glass-active);\n  box-shadow:\n    inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08),\n    0 1px 3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);\n  transition:\n    translate 0.2s ease-in-out,\n    width 0.2s ease-in-out;\n}\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n  .segmented-control-indicator {\n    transition: none;\n  }\n}\nEOF\ncat > src/lib/appearance.ts <<'EOF'\nimport { useCallback, useEffect, useState } from \"react\";\n\n// Settings → Appearance: alternative looks for components, kept side by side\n// while we compare them. The first option of each is the default. When one\n// wins, delete the others and its entry here.\nexport const APPEARANCE_OPTIONS = {\n  viewToggle: [\n    { value: \"pill\", label: \"Pill\" },\n    { value: \"segmented\", label: \"Segmented\" },\n  ],\n} as const;\n\nexport type Appearance = {\n  [Key in keyof typeof APPEARANCE_OPTIONS]: (typeof APPEARANCE_OPTIONS)[Key][number][\"value\"];\n};\n\nconst STORAGE_KEY = \"appearance\";\n\nfunction loadAppearance(): Appearance {\n  let stored: Record<string, unknown> = {};\n  try {\n    stored = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY) ?? \"{}\");\n  } catch {\n    // Unreadable or missing storage keeps the defaults.\n  }\n  const pick = <Key extends keyof Appearance>(key: Key): Appearance[Key] => {\n    const options = APPEARANCE_OPTIONS[key];\n    return (options.find((option) => option.value === stored[key]) ?? options[0]).value;\n  };\n  return { viewToggle: pick(\"viewToggle\") };\n}\n\nexport function useAppearance() {\n  const [appearance, setAppearance] = useState(loadAppearance);\n  useEffect(() => {\n    try {\n      localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(appearance));\n    } catch {\n      return;\n    }\n  }, [appearance]);\n  const setOption = useCallback(\n    <Key extends keyof Appearance>(key: Key, value: Appearance[Key]) =>\n      setAppearance((current) => ({ ...current, [key]: value })),\n    [],\n  );\n  return [appearance, setOption] as const;\n}\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Add segmented control and appearance store"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":321,"cache_read_input_tokens":218286,"output_tokens":6126,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3567},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":321,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6126,"cache_read_input_tokens":218286,"cache_creation_input_tokens":321,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":321},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01L8UCFyf8GkF2eU2Q9Dxh7k":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && cat > src/components/SegmentedControl/SegmentedControl.tsx <<'EOF'\n// The coss ui segmented-control recipe, as published MIT in cosscom/coss\n// packages/kloq @ 4339a256d21a3380745ba054f532e0ec5779930f\n// (src/lib/segmented-control.ts). Copyright (c) 2026 Sean Brydon; see LICENSE.md\n// in this directory. Rebuilt on native radios and plain CSS instead of Base UI\n// and Tailwind. The sliding indicator is inkling's own: the one in coss's\n// packages/ui is AGPL.\n\nimport { type ReactNode, useLayoutEffect, useRef, useState } from \"react\";\nimport \"./SegmentedControl.css\";\n\nexport type SegmentedControlOption<Value extends string> = {\n  value: Value;\n  label: string;\n  icon?: ReactNode;\n};\n\nexport function SegmentedControl<Value extends string>({\n  name,\n  label,\n  options,\n  value,\n  onChange,\n  className,\n}: {\n  /** Groups the radios, so it must be unique on the page. */\n  name: string;\n  /** Read by screen readers; not shown. */\n  label: string;\n  options: readonly SegmentedControlOption<Value>[];\n  value: Value;\n  onChange: (value: Value) => void;\n  className?: string;\n}) {\n  const rootRef = useRef<HTMLFieldSetElement>(null);\n  const [indicator, setIndicator] = useState<{ left: number; width: number } | null>(null);\n\n  useLayoutEffect(() => {\n    const root = rootRef.current;\n    if (!root) return;\n    const measure = () => {\n      const item = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-value=\"${CSS.escape(value)}\"]`);\n      setIndicator(item ? { left: item.offsetLeft, width: item.offsetWidth } : null);\n    };\n    measure();\n    const observer = new ResizeObserver(measure);\n    observer.observe(root);\n    return () => observer.disconnect();\n  }, [value]);\n\n  return (\n    <fieldset ref={rootRef} className={`segmented-control${className ? ` ${className}` : \"\"}`}>\n      <legend className=\"visually-hidden\">{label}</legend>\n      <span\n        className=\"segmented-control-indicator\"\n        aria-hidden=\"true\"\n        hidden={!indicator}\n        style={{ translate: `${indicator?.left ?? 0}px 0`, width: indicator?.width }}\n      />\n      {options.map((option) => (\n        <label\n          key={option.value}\n          className=\"segmented-control-item\"\n          data-value={option.value}\n          data-checked={option.value === value || undefined}\n        >\n          <input\n            type=\"radio\"\n            className=\"visually-hidden\"\n            name={name}\n            value={option.value}\n            checked={option.value === value}\n            onChange={() => onChange(option.value)}\n          />\n          {option.icon}\n          <span>{option.label}</span>\n        </label>\n      ))}\n    </fieldset>\n  );\n}\nEOF\ncat > src/components/SegmentedControl/SegmentedControl.css <<'EOF'\n/* No background of its own: callers add `.glass` or a surface. */\n.segmented-control {\n  position: relative;\n  z-index: 0;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 2px;\n  min-width: 0;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 3px;\n  border: 0;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n}\n.segmented-control-item {\n  position: relative;\n  display: inline-flex;\n  flex: 0 0 auto;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  gap: 6px;\n  height: 28px;\n  padding: 0 11px 0 9px;\n  border-radius: 9px;\n  color: var(--library-muted);\n  cursor: pointer;\n  font: 500 13px / 16px var(--font-ui);\n  white-space: nowrap;\n  user-select: none;\n  transition: color 0.15s ease;\n}\n.segmented-control-item:hover {\n  color: var(--library-text-soft);\n}\n.segmented-control-item[data-checked] {\n  color: var(--library-text);\n}\n.segmented-control-item svg {\n  display: block;\n  flex: 0 0 auto;\n  opacity: 0.8;\n}\n.segmented-control-item[data-checked] svg {\n  opacity: 1;\n}\n.segmented-control-item:has(input:focus-visible) {\n  outline: 2px solid var(--orange);\n  outline-offset: 1px;\n}\n.segmented-control-indicator {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: 3px;\n  bottom: 3px;\n  left: 0;\n  z-index: -1;\n  border-radius: 9px;\n  background: var(--glass-active);\n  box-shadow:\n    inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08),\n    0 1px 3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);\n  transition:\n    translate 0.2s ease-in-out,\n    width 0.2s ease-in-out;\n}\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n  .segmented-control-indicator {\n    transition: none;\n  }\n}\nEOF\ncat > src/lib/appearance.ts <<'EOF'\nimport { useCallback, useEffect, useState } from \"react\";\n\n// Settings → Appearance: alternative looks for components, kept side by side\n// while we compare them. The first option of each is the default. When one\n// wins, delete the others and its entry here.\nexport const APPEARANCE_OPTIONS = {\n  viewToggle: [\n    { value: \"pill\", label: \"Pill\" },\n    { value: \"segmented\", label: \"Segmented\" },\n  ],\n} as const;\n\nexport type Appearance = {\n  [Key in keyof typeof APPEARANCE_OPTIONS]: (typeof APPEARANCE_OPTIONS)[Key][number][\"value\"];\n};\n\nconst STORAGE_KEY = \"appearance\";\n\nfunction loadAppearance(): Appearance {\n  let stored: Record<string, unknown> = {};\n  try {\n    stored = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY) ?? \"{}\");\n  } catch {\n    // Unreadable or missing storage keeps the defaults.\n  }\n  const pick = <Key extends keyof Appearance>(key: Key): Appearance[Key] => {\n    const options = APPEARANCE_OPTIONS[key];\n    return (options.find((option) => option.value === stored[key]) ?? options[0]).value;\n  };\n  return { viewToggle: pick(\"viewToggle\") };\n}\n\nexport function useAppearance() {\n  const [appearance, setAppearance] = useState(loadAppearance);\n  useEffect(() => {\n    try {\n      localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(appearance));\n    } catch {\n      return;\n    }\n  }, [appearance]);\n  const setOption = useCallback(\n    <Key extends keyof Appearance>(key: Key, value: Appearance[Key]) =>\n      setAppearance((current) => ({ ...current, [key]: value })),\n    [],\n  );\n  return [appearance, setOption] as const;\n}\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Add segmented control and appearance store"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01L8UCFyf8GkF2eU2Q9Dxh7k":{"cwd":"/c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgFjWhJG6YYmzEtb8jEvy","requestRef":"165f20ed-dd30-4582-89af-3ddd462c7380","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"4a0c9623-eec1-424f-b8d6-6be494723724","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:56:29.834Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7"