{"parentUuid":"535dcefc-44dd-4e07-a5e9-c63039115326","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"761638c0-aa7a-4fa6-accf-c8ca2c05ada7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KdQFPVD4mBxWAaZdPEVxUM","type":"tool_result","content":"# Vendored bloub engine (`src/components/mascot/bot/`)\r\n\r\nSource: https://github.com/jeremy-prt/bloub by Jérémy Perret, MIT licensed.\r\nNot affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to x.ai.\r\n\r\n## What this is\r\n\r\n`src/bot/` from bloub is framework-free and clock-free: `BotEngine.sample(t)`\r\nis a pure function of time. Only this directory was vendored — the Vue shell\r\n(`BloubBot.vue`, views, i18n, export pipeline) was deliberately left behind and\r\nre-implemented in React as `../InklingMascot.tsx`.\r\n\r\n## Rules for this directory\r\n\r\n- Keep it pure: no `Date.now()`, no React/Vue imports. React adapters live\r\n  one level up. This preserves frozen-frame rendering and DOM-less testing.\r\n- `profiles.ts` is measured reference data — never edit by hand.\r\n- `skins.ts` is the sanctioned extension point for inkling shapes and colors\r\n  (marked `INKLING EXTENSION`). Adding a shape there also registers it in the\r\n  `eyefit.ts` correction table built at import.\r\n- New animations go in `states.ts` as new `StateDef` entries; never rewrite\r\n  measured states. Blocks hold or cut time, never scale it (`cycles.ts`).\r\n- The engine (`engine.ts`) may gain small declarative, default-off state flags\r\n  (like `steadyFace`); never per-frame behavior changes that could disturb the\r\n  measured states.\r\n- Test files (`*.test.ts`) were not vendored (vitest + happy-dom); equivalent\r\n  coverage for inkling shapes lives in `../inklingSkins.test.ts` (bun:test).\r\nsrc/App.tsx\nsrc/components/GradualBlur/GradualBlur.tsx\nsrc/components/mascot/MascotBoard.tsx\nsrc/components/SegmentedControl/SegmentedControl.tsx\nelectron/ai-jobs.mjs:144:        \"Loading local Nomic embedding models\",\nelectron/embedding-contract.mjs:1:export const TEXT_MODEL = \"nomic-embed-text-v1.5\";\nelectron/embedding-contract.mjs:5:export const IMAGE_MODEL = \"nomic-embed-vision-v1.5-sharp\";\nelectron/ai-jobs.test.ts:196:      body: \"## Nomic\\n\\nA **local** model.\",\nelectron/ai-jobs.test.ts:201:  ).toBe(\"Reading list\\n\\nNomic A local model.\\n\\nCover text\");\nelectron/embeddings.test.ts:39:  expect(TEXT_MODEL).toBe(\"nomic-embed-text-v1.5\");\nelectron/embeddings.test.ts:40:  expect(IMAGE_MODEL).toBe(\"nomic-embed-vision-v1.5-sharp\");\nbuild:\nicon.icns\nicon.ico\nicon.png\n\npublic:\nseed-demo\nvite.svg","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5bd8db23-15f1-478f-b2f0-94b9ccb99027","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:01:57.663Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Vendored bloub engine (`src/components/mascot/bot/`)\r\n\r\nSource: https://github.com/jeremy-prt/bloub by Jérémy Perret, MIT licensed.\r\nNot affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to x.ai.\r\n\r\n## What this is\r\n\r\n`src/bot/` from bloub is framework-free and clock-free: `BotEngine.sample(t)`\r\nis a pure function of time. Only this directory was vendored — the Vue shell\r\n(`BloubBot.vue`, views, i18n, export pipeline) was deliberately left behind and\r\nre-implemented in React as `../InklingMascot.tsx`.\r\n\r\n## Rules for this directory\r\n\r\n- Keep it pure: no `Date.now()`, no React/Vue imports. React adapters live\r\n  one level up. This preserves frozen-frame rendering and DOM-less testing.\r\n- `profiles.ts` is measured reference data — never edit by hand.\r\n- `skins.ts` is the sanctioned extension point for inkling shapes and colors\r\n  (marked `INKLING EXTENSION`). Adding a shape there also registers it in the\r\n  `eyefit.ts` correction table built at import.\r\n- New animations go in `states.ts` as new `StateDef` entries; never rewrite\r\n  measured states. Blocks hold or cut time, never scale it (`cycles.ts`).\r\n- The engine (`engine.ts`) may gain small declarative, default-off state flags\r\n  (like `steadyFace`); never per-frame behavior changes that could disturb the\r\n  measured states.\r\n- Test files (`*.test.ts`) were not vendored (vitest + happy-dom); equivalent\r\n  coverage for inkling shapes lives in `../inklingSkins.test.ts` (bun:test).\r\nsrc/App.tsx\nsrc/components/GradualBlur/GradualBlur.tsx\nsrc/components/mascot/MascotBoard.tsx\nsrc/components/SegmentedControl/SegmentedControl.tsx\nelectron/ai-jobs.mjs:144:        \"Loading local Nomic embedding models\",\nelectron/embedding-contract.mjs:1:export const TEXT_MODEL = \"nomic-embed-text-v1.5\";\nelectron/embedding-contract.mjs:5:export const IMAGE_MODEL = \"nomic-embed-vision-v1.5-sharp\";\nelectron/ai-jobs.test.ts:196:      body: \"## Nomic\\n\\nA **local** model.\",\nelectron/ai-jobs.test.ts:201:  ).toBe(\"Reading list\\n\\nNomic A local model.\\n\\nCover text\");\nelectron/embeddings.test.ts:39:  expect(TEXT_MODEL).toBe(\"nomic-embed-text-v1.5\");\nelectron/embeddings.test.ts:40:  expect(IMAGE_MODEL).toBe(\"nomic-embed-vision-v1.5-sharp\");\nbuild:\nicon.icns\nicon.ico\nicon.png\n\npublic:\nseed-demo\nvite.svg","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"535dcefc-44dd-4e07-a5e9-c63039115326","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
