{"parentUuid":"9614ac8e-ca40-44c7-862c-cc8755042132","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01V48mWhwpTDjHKabkzWuM3P","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"bc259db6-80a9-44dd-b302-ad2f6a3503c4","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:02:28.255Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"bc259db6-80a9-44dd-b302-ad2f6a3503c4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFjzse9NPXzGkpYUbTUF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Since the bundled models (Nomic, Tesseract) are Apache-2.0 licensed and shipped with the app, I need to account for Electron's runtime license too — adding a custom notice with the MIT text from Electron's LICENSE file, and considering whether to reference the Chromium licenses file that electron-builder includes in the app directory.\n\nI'm now sketching a script to actually collect these third-party licenses automatically: traversing root package.json dependencies plus the workspace package's deps, resolving each package's actual directory on disk (accounting for Bun's hoisted or isolated node_modules layout and following symlinks), then reading each package's license field or license file to build a manifest.\n\nI also realize there are vendored components without proper LICENSE files included -- like the GradualBlur and segmented control components -- so I'm planning a supplementary notices config listing those manually with their source license files or inline notice text, since the generator alone won't catch bundled/copied code.\n\nFor Apache-2.0 licensed items like the Nomic models, I don't think there's a vendored LICENSE file to reuse, so I'll vendor the Apache 2.0 text once myself and reference it from the notices config rather than trying to hack together a copy from node_modules.\n\nFor the plugin, I'm deciding to emit the licenses JSON during build via `generateBundle`, but also add a dev server middleware that generates it on-the-fly so the settings page doesn't 404 when running locally — since scanning node_modules is cheap enough. I also need to make sure the manifest covers both the renderer bundle and the Electron main process dependencies like sharp, onnxruntime-node, canvas, and tesseract, since those ship too even though they're not bundled into the renderer. Now I'm adding a row to the Settings General tab for open source licenses.\n\nI'm designing the licenses sub-page with a breadcrumb back button, a header showing count and search, and a list of expandable rows showing name, version, license, and notice text — using native details/summary for simplicity, with content only rendered when expanded to keep ~400 rows performant. For source links I need to check how the app currently handles opening external URLs in Electron, since clicking a link should use shell.openExternal via preload rather than a plain anchor tag.\n\nFor documentation I'll add a short explanatory comment in the generator script itself plus a changelog line rather than a separate docs file, and I'll write a bun test that spins up a fixture node_modules directory to verify the generator follows dependencies, dedupes packages, picks the right license files, and flags any missing licenses — also need to double check bun's node_modules layout and whether knip will complain about the script not being imported anywhere besides vite.config.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":957,"cache_read_input_tokens":255213,"output_tokens":2237,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1952},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":957,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2237,"cache_read_input_tokens":255213,"cache_creation_input_tokens":957,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":957},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":24047,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFjzsLHD1eexq6uscpPW","requestRef":"b9bf9f9a-9a0c-4383-ac7f-7a5997d54d6f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e98d449a-7188-4828-a438-8861b9e9371c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:02:28.254Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"e98d449a-7188-4828-a438-8861b9e9371c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFjzse9NPXzGkpYUbTUF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All dependencies are npm packages except a few vendored pieces (GradualBlur, the segmented control, the bloub mascot engine, and the bundled Nomic models). Now I'll check how Bun structures `node_modules` so the generator can traverse it properly.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":957,"cache_read_input_tokens":255213,"output_tokens":2237,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1952},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":957,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2237,"cache_read_input_tokens":255213,"cache_creation_input_tokens":957,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":957},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgFjzsLHD1eexq6uscpPW","requestRef":"b9bf9f9a-9a0c-4383-ac7f-7a5997d54d6f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"52962118-8495-47f7-b6bf-84c573ba8027","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:02:28.267Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
