{"parentUuid":"794f8f9b-bf2c-421b-a501-4981be7c4ef6","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01XijBcZwEYZAWveiALGzNad","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"88d790f8-cb7a-4968-9a78-643af49306fe","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:03:36.144Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"88d790f8-cb7a-4968-9a78-643af49306fe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFk4xk5ZvN34cT5pXVEH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm writing the collector script that gathers third-party license data for Settings → General → Open source licenses, scanning node_modules for the production dependency closure plus manually tracked notices.\n\nNow I'm working through the tricky part of resolving nested package locations in Bun's node_modules layout, since walking up from a package's realpath doesn't match Node's normal resolution rules and I need to handle that carefully to avoid generating wrong paths.\n\nI'm also sketching out a helper to extract license info from a package.json, handling both string licenses and license objects with a type field.\n\nThen I need a function to derive a source URL from the repository field or homepage, normalizing various git URL shorthand formats into proper https github links, and a separate step for reading notice files that match a naming pattern, sorted and concatenated.\n\nNow I'm sketching the main license-collection routine: it walks the dependency tree from the root package.json, including shipped dev dependencies, using a queue-based traversal that tracks visited directories by real path and records any packages whose install location can't be found as missing.\n\nI'm also working through how first-party `@inkling/` workspace packages resolve via symlinks in node_modules back to their actual package directories, so their own dependencies still get walked even though the packages themselves are skipped from the third-party license list, and I'm noting that some optional dependencies (like platform-specific native binaries) are expected to be missing and shouldn't be flagged as errors.\n\nFor peer dependencies, I'll follow any that are actually installed but not treat a missing peer as fatal, since they're usually satisfied elsewhere in the dependency tree already. I'm defining the entry shape for each package (name, version, license, source URL, notice text, kind) and deciding that packages without a license file get an empty notice string plus a warning surfaced back to the caller so the UI can flag it.\n\nFor custom notices I'll read the JSON file listing them and pull in each notice's text directly from disk. I'm sorting the final manifest case-insensitively by name, keeping custom entries (no version) mixed into the same list rather than a separate section, and estimating the output size is fine for on-demand loading rather than startup — a few hundred KB at most across packages and font OFL texts. Now I'm writing the Vite plugin that builds this third-party-licenses.json file during the build step.\n\nWriting plugin dev-server middleware...\n\nThen I need to make sure the renderer can actually fetch this file correctly given Electron's app:// protocol and how Vite resolves the base path for assets.\n\nFor the UI, I'm planning the Settings General row for open source licenses—picking an icon and drafting the heading and description text explaining that inkling is built with software, fonts, and models from others.\n\nI'm building a dedicated OpenSourceLicenses component with a back button, header, notice count, search field, and list, keeping it separate from App for cleanliness, and wiring up the settings tab state and sidebar highlighting so it works alongside the General tab. Setting up the license entry type and a cached loader function to fetch the data...\n\nStill writing fetch logic...\n\nNow I'm designing the expandable row markup for each license entry, with a toggle button showing a chevron, name, version, and license id, plus an optional external source link.\n\nFor styling I'm planning monospace fonts for ids/versions, hairline separators between rows matching the settings panel style, hover backgrounds, and a scrollable pre block for notice text. I'm also adding content-visibility optimizations since there could be hundreds of rows, and sketching out an error state message.\n\nI'm thinking through dev middleware serving licenses, writing a test file for collect.mjs with bun test, and verifying the Electron protocol handler can serve the JSON fine regardless of MIME type. I still need to check which hugeicons license icon is available to use in the settings row.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1207,"cache_read_input_tokens":261041,"output_tokens":3937,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3586},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1207,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3937,"cache_read_input_tokens":261041,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1207,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1207},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":36523,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFk4xPzqbGQEcUXqPKcu","requestRef":"04e8d459-5657-4c06-aae0-42b806c3b7ae","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"97e32987-71df-46b5-92ab-2c52b4fe0e96","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:03:36.144Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
