{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","prNumber":170,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Squidys-Tools/inkling/pull/170","prRepository":"Squidys-Tools/inkling","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:08:48.444Z"}
{"parentUuid":"a3dc46c5-24fd-4640-bd80-0ab2ae690348","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"761638c0-aa7a-4fa6-accf-c8ca2c05ada7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PZ7Uax6ELZ2XFKR1nVAona","type":"tool_result","content":"The operation completed successfully.\r\r\n## Unreleased\n\n### Added\n\n- Settings → Appearance switches components between alternative looks while we compare them, starting with the grid/list toggle as the current pill or a coss ui segmented control (#170)\n- First-run welcome flow on first launch of the installed app, replayable from Settings → General\n- PDF cards now show page-one thumbnails generated in the background after capture; existing PDFs are backfilled one at a time when the job queue is idle.\n- Chrome MV3 extension saves a page or right-clicked link through inkling's local capture receiver, with the existing capture link as fallback.\n- `bun run ui:smoke` drives the core library flows in Electron against a scratch profile and fails on console errors\n- Electron desktop shell alongside Tauri, with scoped `app://` assets, an IPC command allowlist, and `inkling://` capture links.\n- Electron now opens the shared schema-v8 SQLite library with search, Spaces, archive, backup/restore, and a persisted job queue running local OCR, PDF extraction, and Nomic embeddings.\n- Electron now accepts authenticated browser-extension saves over a loopback server and stores URL deep links before processing runs.\n- Electron now ships with a Windows NSIS installer, bundled local models, and a generic GitHub Release update feed; unsigned installers and updates may trigger SmartScreen warnings.\n- The packaged Tauri Windows app checks GitHub for signed updates at launch and offers user-controlled installation from the sidebar; its NSIS installer remains unsigned and may trigger a SmartScreen warning (SQU-16).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ce160e38-eaba-4a87-828e-f7005febb62f","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:08:48.799Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"The operation completed successfully.\r\r\n## Unreleased\n\n### Added\n\n- Settings → Appearance switches components between alternative looks while we compare them, starting with the grid/list toggle as the current pill or a coss ui segmented control (#170)\n- First-run welcome flow on first launch of the installed app, replayable from Settings → General\n- PDF cards now show page-one thumbnails generated in the background after capture; existing PDFs are backfilled one at a time when the job queue is idle.\n- Chrome MV3 extension saves a page or right-clicked link through inkling's local capture receiver, with the existing capture link as fallback.\n- `bun run ui:smoke` drives the core library flows in Electron against a scratch profile and fails on console errors\n- Electron desktop shell alongside Tauri, with scoped `app://` assets, an IPC command allowlist, and `inkling://` capture links.\n- Electron now opens the shared schema-v8 SQLite library with search, Spaces, archive, backup/restore, and a persisted job queue running local OCR, PDF extraction, and Nomic embeddings.\n- Electron now accepts authenticated browser-extension saves over a loopback server and stores URL deep links before processing runs.\n- Electron now ships with a Windows NSIS installer, bundled local models, and a generic GitHub Release update feed; unsigned installers and updates may trigger SmartScreen warnings.\n- The packaged Tauri Windows app checks GitHub for signed updates at launch and offers user-controlled installation from the sidebar; its NSIS installer remains unsigned and may trigger a SmartScreen warning (SQU-16).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a3dc46c5-24fd-4640-bd80-0ab2ae690348","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf