{"parentUuid":"9900837e-49d0-4f33-94b1-ee96e0120f63","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[{"name":"mcp__claude_ai_Unsplash__add_asset_to_collection","description":"Add a photo or illustration to a collection. Find the asset with `search_photos` or `search_illustrations`, and obtain or create the destination collection before calling this tool.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"collection_id":{"type":"string"},"asset_id":{"type":"string","description":"The `id` of a photo or illustration returned by an asset search or collection tool."}},"required":["collection_id","asset_id"],"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__col__render_component","description":"Show the user a live, interactive render of a component inside the chat, after choosing it with search_components and get_component. Write the module for the user's real use case (their labels, layout, and theme), not a generic demo. Packages load from esm.sh at render time; Col bundles none. In Claude Code, which does not show MCP Apps, pass format 'html' and show the returned fragment with an inline HTML widget tool, or open it in the browser. This server is read-only and never requests or stores credentials.","input_schema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","type":"object","properties":{"code":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":50000,"description":"One self-contained TSX module whose default export is a React component showing the chosen component in the user's own use case. Import packages by npm name, optionally pinned ('@mantine/core@9.7.1'); they load from esm.sh with React 19 shared. Import package CSS directly ('@mantine/core/styles.css'). Tailwind utility classes work. Relative and '@/' imports fail: inline local files such as shadcn's components/ui sources. Use synthetic sample data only."},"format":{"description":"'widget' (default) renders through MCP Apps. 'html' also returns the same render as a self-contained HTML fragment, for hosts that cannot show MCP Apps, such as Claude Code: pass it to an inline HTML widget tool (e.g. show_widget), or save it as an .html file that starts with '<!doctype html><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\">' and open it in the browser.","type":"string","enum":["widget","html"]}},"required":["code"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b2a337b7-4feb-45f7-b908-e8aaea37a46e","timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:58:25.508Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
