{"parentUuid":"bd062258-52cc-4af2-b719-3813c7b40844","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFqYNPiiS3sLkSaeH8b1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm thinking about rendering a single shared context menu component rather than one per card, using event delegation on the library grid container to find which item was right-clicked and open the menu at the pointer location, while keeping the separate archive grid's context handling untouched.\n\nFor menu contents, I'm planning items like Open, Star/Unstar, visiting the source link, copying the link, showing in folder (desktop only), and Archive — deferring the \"Add to Space\" submenu for a later pass. I'm also working through keyboard accessibility: handling the context menu key via onContextMenu, positioning and clamping the menu within the viewport, closing on Escape/outside click/scroll/blur/resize, arrow-key navigation between items, and restoring focus to the card when the menu closes, using proper menu/menuitem roles throughout.\n\nCopy link can use the clipboard API since Electron's app:// context supports it, with a quick toast confirming the copy. For show-in-folder and opening the original source, I need to check the existing overlay handlers' signatures to reuse them, then locate where the main grid context gets defined.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2384,"cache_read_input_tokens":153496,"output_tokens":874,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":692},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2384,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":874,"cache_read_input_tokens":153496,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2384,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_inp