{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"c4b0f3c4b33e1aec9f375b0aa6022d4c9e96e7ac5855749fd3ed1e6209ef3d70","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm wiring up the context menu into the App, adding an onOpenMenu callback to the card context so right-clicking a card triggers a menu with position and target info tracked in state.\n\nNow I'm fleshing out the menu entries: Open, Read (if applicable), Star/Unstar via togglePinItem, a separator, then host-based actions like opening the source URL, copying the link, and showing in folder on desktop, followed by another separator and an Archive option using forgetItem. I'm checking that all these handler functions are defined earlier in the file so they're available, and confirming the pin state and favorite status come from the live item data. For placement, since the menu is a portal I can mount it anywhere in the JSX, so I'm deciding to put it near the Toaster component toward the end of App.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H3pLxGjQD1ZcY9hkKSZuza","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && grep -n \"<Toaster\" src/App.tsx; grep -n \"^  StarIcon,\\|^  Copy01Icon\\|^  Folder01Icon\\|^  Archive01Icon\\|^  BookOpen01Icon\\|^  LinkSquare02Icon\\|^  ViewIcon\\|^  Maximize01Icon\" src/App.tsx; grep -n \"hostnameForUrl\" src/App.tsx src/lib/*.ts | head -3; grep -n \"type ReaderOrigin\" -A3 src/App.tsx src/*.ts* | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019Y7BGppVWPezmFZwH14R5r","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304\\src\\App.tsx","offset":2376,"limit":30},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
