{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"78799904c734e6ed87f3f4b43dcfa3df309643b9bd3002f4c481c6f60844ee34","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm trying to pin down where the blue scroller-top line falls relative to the library header and frame offsets in the screenshot, estimating it lands near the top of the reachable scroll area.\n\nWorking out the resting scroll offset so cards align with that blue line — roughly 52px seems right for the plain case, but I'm less sure about the pinned-query case since the filter row might overlap the grid rather than sit above it. I'll just test whether using the same offset for both scenarios lands the cards at the blue line consistently.\n\nNow I need to figure out where the app actually resets scroll position — searching for where scrollTop gets set to zero, and confirming whether `.library-grid` is the real scroller or if `.library-scroll` wraps it. I'm considering a CSS scroll-snap approach but it feels fragile, so instead I'll write a small helper function that explicitly sets the rest scroll position on the correct element.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L26GNfUjr9RzxY4Cq1jBgR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && grep -n \"scrollTop\\b\\|scrollTo(\\|scrollTop =\" src/App.tsx | head -40; grep -n \"className=\\\"library-scroll\\|library-grid\" src/App.tsx | head -20"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
