{"parentUuid":"f429838a-3b31-49e6-be54-4e1a3cd0dbc3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFvxNTwdUSunsgSAhmyb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm thinking the same Virtuoso instance likely persists scroll position across grid/list switches, so I should apply the rest offset logic consistently for both views using a layout effect keyed on the grid key, while being careful that setting scrollTop too early—before Virtuoso has measured content height—could cause clamping issues.\n\nWith sparse item counts there may not even be enough scroll room for the offset to apply, so cards could sit lower than intended; I'm considering adding a minimum height to the grid's inner content to guarantee scroll room exists. I also want to check Virtuoso's masonry DOM structure directly in the running app, and look into whether retrying the scrollTop set across multiple frames (or an initialScrollTop prop) would solve the async measurement timing problem.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1190,"cache_read_input_tokens":204765,"output_tokens":785,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":617},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1190,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":785,"cache_read_input_tokens":204765,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1190,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1190},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":9589,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFvxN57ufTDYgSjm8GDG","requestRef":"3f1e08b8-dc78-4587-9df0-29706f1cc