{"parentUuid":"3cd89b85-f77e-433f-b9d9-44970fe3015f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01KC1AZ1MhQTFy6gwqvg4rKG","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e94aa62d-772b-49cf-b7f1-c976696e1bdc","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:26:31.266Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"e94aa62d-772b-49cf-b7f1-c976696e1bdc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFvzRvrNsaDnWzQomiwV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm calculating the scroll offset by comparing the blue reference line position to the scroller's top padding, landing on an offset of 52 so the card aligns correctly. Now I need to check whether the grid's children are styled as flex columns to understand how the layout will respond.\n\nFor extra scroll room, I'm exploring whether adding min-height to the grid columns based on percentage calculations against the scroller's content box could force the scroll height past the required threshold—but I realize Virtuoso likely sets inline heights that would conflict with this approach.\n\nInstead I'm leaning toward programmatically setting scrollTop after mount via useLayoutEffect, since the min-height guarantee ensures the room exists by the time the DOM is ready. I also need to handle the pinned-query case where padding differs (112px), and I'm deciding to define a shared rest-offset constant—likely as a CSS variable on the scroll container—so both the JS scrollTop logic and the CSS calculations stay in sync rather than duplicating the magic number.\n\nI'm now checking other places that reset scroll position, like view switching and the close-scroll-into-view behavior, and those seem already handled correctly. But I'm realizing a problem: the top GradualBlur band is 96px tall, so cards resting at the 52px line would actually sit under that blur — meaning the \"rest\" position the user wants might visually look blurred, which contradicts their expectation that the blur only appears during scroll.\n\nMaybe setting hoverIntensity to 1 is the fix to stop hover from clearing the blur — that could be what they mean by \"autohide\" behavior. Now I need to look at the thumbnail bug in list mode, where the thumbnail falls short of the card bottom by about 10px, which means checking the list-mode CSS for the media element.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1606,"cache_read_input_tokens":206965,"output_tokens":1446,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1302},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1606,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1446,"cache_read_input_tokens":206965,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1606,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1606},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":18279,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFvzRc1bvj8c82Digs4C","requestRef":"a8427835-7dbf-45d4-9624-51bbdacf9416","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"921ab45a-3076-4de3-b2b2-fc2bff0bbf98","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:26:31.266Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
