{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"ead43058d9716f39275a943f877b5f574e1ca7adeb62b7ba875c16fcc1668baa","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's no explicit user setting here — it's about automatic support detection, using liquid glass where available and falling back to CSS glass otherwise. The tricky part is that tooltips need to match this style too, but liquid glass only renders properly over the library stage content, while tooltips can appear over the sidebar as well, so I need to think about whether tooltips tied to stage elements like the dock or capture bar could register as liquid glass targets despite being transient and freely positioned.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xup7tUSQeySPjmRacNgbr5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && sed -n 1,120p src/components/LiquidGlass.tsx"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0172QDKatA47C1XC94sjaCBo","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && sed -n 120,520p src/components/LiquidGlass.tsx"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
