{"parentUuid":"3ea6d77f-8828-464c-88ed-1fafd35b16cf","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01Xup7tUSQeySPjmRacNgbr5","copy":"wire"},{"id":"toolu_0172QDKatA47C1XC94sjaCBo","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7b90ec09-9723-4a0a-ae29-5313ab112bb2","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:34:55.826Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"7b90ec09-9723-4a0a-ae29-5313ab112bb2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFwdmkF42vV1pjq9deeC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm thinking about how glass targets need to be within observed root subtrees, so a tooltip rendered via portal would need its own dedicated layer—maybe a fixed-position overlay div with pointer-events disabled that gets included as one of the watched roots.\n\nTooltips over the canvas stage could get liquid glass since glassShape clips to that area, but tooltips over the sidebar would likely fall outside the shape and just fall back to CSS glass, which seems like an acceptable behavior split. I also need to confirm whether the tooltip layer actually sits inside the LiquidGlass container hierarchy for this to work.\n\nThe tooltip layer needs to live outside the canvas, probably as a fixed-position sibling at the app-shell level so positioning isn't affected by any transforms in main-content. I'm planning a global delegated tooltip system: a TooltipLayer component that listens for pointerover/focusin on elements with a data-tooltip attribute, applies hover/focus delay logic, and hides on pointerout, escape, scroll, or pointerdown, positioning the tooltip relative to the target element.\n\nNow I'm working out positioning details -- centering below the element with a gap, flipping above when near the bottom edge, clamping horizontally, and measuring the tooltip in a layout effect. For accessibility I'm deciding to mark the tooltip as aria-hidden since elements already have aria-labels, avoiding duplication. Then I need to audit existing title= attributes across components and replace them with data-tooltip, making sure not to leave both since that would cause native tooltips to double up with the new custom ones.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7660,"cache_read_input_tokens":242257,"output_tokens":1377,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1206},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7660,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1377,"cache_read_input_tokens":242257,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7660,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7660},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":16272,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFwdmT99mMZXxyzAWViD","requestRef":"1f9766e1-ff68-4d9e-84ce-e401f7b825d7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d184efdb-f562-437d-b11c-d2dbd053d835","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:34:55.825Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
