{"parentUuid":"998117e1-64cb-4849-acdf-b4afe8373869","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_014iPknkKpBhYGGwuzaUrZ8g","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"616a003a-23a0-4e61-88bd-f22eac9f8ae9","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:35:33.670Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"616a003a-23a0-4e61-88bd-f22eac9f8ae9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFwgefSAL8iYmZGWkF8M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm worried about tooltips that straddle the sidebar edge getting rendered with a half-invisible liquid glass effect, since the portion outside the canvas wouldn't draw. I should mitigate this in the TooltipLayer by only marking a tooltip as fully off-canvas when it's completely outside the sidebar bounds, falling back to CSS glass otherwise.\n\nThere's also a small risk of a one-frame flash when a tooltip first appears, since it gets marked transparent via data-liquid before the canvas paints its shape—likely acceptable given the brief duration and existing fade-in/settle polling behavior.\n\nActually I realize overlays complicate things: an overlay sits above the library stage, so a liquid tooltip positioned over the overlay would incorrectly refract the hidden library grid behind it rather than the overlay's own content. The fix is to restrict liquid glass to tooltips whose anchor lives within specific chrome regions, like the capture bar or view dock, checking with a closest() selector rather than just testing full containment within the stage rect.\n\nThis matches where glass is used elsewhere, so I'll move forward and start writing TooltipLayer.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1460,"cache_read_input_tokens":254942,"output_tokens":3217,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1036},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1460,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3217,"cache_read_input_tokens":254942,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1460,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1460},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":14973,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFwgeJ71vARUR5CZhfXT","requestRef":"5c001084-9f86-4e2c-af22-c72f2237ca11","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"346241b0-2d70-44a2-893f-385779b997dd","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:35:33.668Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"346241b0-2d70-44a2-893f-385779b997dd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFwgefSAL8iYmZGWkF8M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Since liquid glass only refracts what's behind it, I'll reserve it for tooltips over the toolbar and view dock, using CSS glass everywhere else to avoid distorting the wrong content. Now writing the tooltip layer.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1460,"cache_read_input_tokens":254942,"output_tokens":3217,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1036},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1460,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3217,"cache_read_input_tokens":254942,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1460,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1460},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgFwgeJ71vARUR5CZhfXT","requestRef":"5c001084-9f86-4e2c-af22-c72f2237ca11","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b5eb95df-873e-4c4b-883e-62e6aa164285","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:35:33.685Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"b5eb95df-873e-4c4b-883e-62e6aa164285","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFwgefSAL8iYmZGWkF8M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WSd6Lm3k6fEoyA2Srh47VE","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304\\src\\components\\Tooltip\\TooltipLayer.tsx","content":"import { type RefObject, useEffect, useLayoutEffect, useRef, useState } from \"react\";\nimport \"./Tooltip.css\";\n\n// One tooltip for the whole app. Controls opt in with `data-tooltip=\"…\"` (in\n// place of `title`, whose native tooltip is slow and ignores the theme), and\n// this layer shows it on hover after a beat, or at once on keyboard focus.\n// Moving straight from one control to the next skips the wait.\n\nconst SHOW_DELAY_MS = 500;\n// Within this long of one tooltip closing, the next opens without the delay.\nconst SKIP_DELAY_MS = 400;\nconst GAP = 8;\nconst EDGE = 6;\n// Anchors in this chrome sit over the library stage, where liquid glass can\n// draw the tooltip (LiquidGlass.tsx). Anywhere else the stage is not behind\n// it, so it keeps the CSS glass.\nconst LIQUID_ANCHORS = \".capture-bar, .view-dock\";\n\ntype Tip = { anchor: HTMLElement; text: string };\n\nexport function TooltipLayer({ ref }: { ref: RefObject<HTMLDivElement | null> }) {\n  const [tip, setTip] = useState<Tip | null>(null);\n  const tipRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);\n  const [placement, setPlacement] = useState<{ left: number; top: number } | null>(null);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    let timer = 0;\n    let closedAt = 0;\n    let current: HTMLElement | null = null;\n    const show = (anchor: HTMLElement, immediate: boolean) => {\n      const text = anchor.dataset.tooltip;\n      if (!text) return;\n      current = anchor;\n      window.clearTimeout(timer);\n      const open = () => setTip({ anchor, text });\n      if (immediate || performance.now() - closedAt < SKIP_DELAY_MS) open();\n      else timer = window.setTimeout(open, SHOW_DELAY_MS);\n    };\n    const hide = () => {\n      window.clearTimeout(timer);\n      if (current) closedAt = performance.now();\n      current = null;\n      setTip(null);\n    };\n    const anchorOf = (target: EventTarget | null) =>\n      target instanceof Element ? target.closest<HTMLElement>(\"[data-tooltip]\") : null;\n\n    const onOver = (event: PointerEvent) => {\n      if (event.pointerType === \"touch\") return;\n      const anchor = anchorOf(event.target);\n      if (anchor === current) return;\n      if (current) hide();\n      if (anchor) show(anchor, false);\n    };\n    const onOut = (event: PointerEvent) => {\n      if (!current) return;\n      const next = event.relatedTarget;\n      if (next instanceof Node && current.contains(next)) return;\n      hide();\n    };\n    const onFocus = (event: FocusEvent) => {\n      const anchor = anchorOf(event.target);\n      if (anchor && anchor === event.target && anchor.matches(\":focus-visible\")) show(anchor, true);\n    };\n    const onKey = (event: KeyboardEvent) => {\n      if (event.key === \"Escape\") hide();\n    };\n\n    document.addEventListener(\"pointerover\", onOver);\n    document.addEventListener(\"pointerout\", onOut);\n    document.addEventListener(\"focusin\", onFocus);\n    document.addEventListener(\"focusout\", hide);\n    document.addEventListener(\"pointerdown\", hide, true);\n    document.addEventListener(\"keydown\", onKey, true);\n    window.addEventListener(\"wheel\", hide, { capture: true, passive: true });\n    window.addEventListener(\"blur\", hide);\n    return () => {\n      window.clearTimeout(timer);\n      document.removeEventListener(\"pointerover\", onOver);\n      document.removeEventListener(\"pointerout\", onOut);\n      document.removeEventListener(\"focusin\", onFocus);\n      document.removeEventListener(\"focusout\", hide);\n      document.removeEventListener(\"pointerdown\", hide, true);\n      document.removeEventListener(\"keydown\", onKey, true);\n      window.removeEventListener(\"wheel\", hide, true);\n      window.removeEventListener(\"blur\", hide);\n    };\n  }, []);\n\n  // A control whose label changes while hovered (Star → Unstar) updates in place.\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (!tip) return;\n    const observer = new MutationObserver(() => {\n      const text = tip.anchor.dataset.tooltip;\n      if (!text || !tip.anchor.isConnected) setTip(null);\n      else if (text !== tip.text) setTip({ ...tip, text });\n    });\n    observer.observe(tip.anchor, { attributes: true, attributeFilter: [\"data-tooltip\"] });\n    return () => observer.disconnect();\n  }, [tip]);\n\n  // Below the control, or above it when there is no room (the view dock).\n  useLayoutEffect(() => {\n    const element = tipRef.current;\n    if (!tip || !element) {\n      setPlacement(null);\n      return;\n    }\n    const anchor = tip.anchor.getBoundingClientRect();\n    const { width, height } = element.getBoundingClientRect();\n    const below = anchor.bottom + GAP;\n    const top =\n      below + height > window.innerHeight - EDGE ? anchor.top - GAP - height : below;\n    const left = Math.min(\n      Math.max(EDGE, anchor.left + anchor.width / 2 - width / 2),\n      window.innerWidth - EDGE - width,\n    );\n    setPlacement({ left, top });\n  }, [tip]);\n\n  const liquid = tip?.anchor.closest(LIQUID_ANCHORS) != null;\n  return (\n    <div ref={ref} className=\"tooltip-layer\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n      {tip && (\n        <div\n          ref={tipRef}\n          className={`tooltip ${liquid ? \"glass\" : \"css-glass\"}`}\n          style={placement ?? { visibility: \"hidden\" }}\n        >\n          {tip.text}\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1460,"cache_read_input_tokens":254942,"output_tokens":3217,"output_tok