{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"aac583f987adeab93e573afa8c7b2cc18671208b7687b4fc1dcd4f434cb0c034","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm trimming the context menu to drop \"Open,\" rename \"star,\" and remove separators, then adjusting the edge tab CSS so the closed state matches the open state's opacity, with corners restored to 14px, slightly smaller dimensions, and the background/border/shadow mirrored for the right-side closed position.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Next, the context menu and edge tab changes:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014n8iHouPUmdEaKP2g7jrAe","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && cat > /tmp/edit3.py <<'EOF'\nimport io\np='src/App.tsx'\ns=io.open(p,encoding='utf8',newline='').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1, a\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep('''    const entries: ContextMenuEntry[] = [\n      {\n        label: \"Open\",\n        icon: ViewIcon,\n        onSelect: () => selectLibraryItem(item, cardRectsFor(card)),\n      },\n    ];''','''    const entries: ContextMenuEntry[] = [];''')\nrep('''      label: item.favorite ? \"Unstar\" : \"Star to Top of mind\",''','''      label: item.favorite ? \"Unfavorite\" : \"Favorite\",''')\nrep('''    if (sourceUrl || canUseDesktopBackend) entries.push(\"separator\");\n''','')\nrep('''    entries.push(\"separator\", {\n      label: \"Archive\",''','''    entries.push({\n      label: \"Archive\",''')\nio.open(p,'w',encoding='utf8',newline='').write(s)\np='src/App.css'\ns=io.open(p,encoding='utf8',newline='').read()\nrep('''    top: 25px;\n    left: 0;\n    z-index: 32;\n    display: grid;\n    place-items: center;\n    width: 32px;\n    height: 46px;''','''    top: 26px;\n    left: 0;\n    z-index: 32;\n    display: grid;\n    place-items: center;\n    width: 30px;\n    height: 44px;''')\nrep('''  /* Open: a solid tab hanging off the frame's edge over the sidebar. */\n  .edge-tab.is-open {\n    --flip: 90deg;\n    margin-left: -31px;\n    border: 1px solid var(--library-border);\n    border-right: 0;\n    border-radius: 20px 0 0 20px / 23px 0 0 23px;\n    background: var(--library-frame);\n    box-shadow:\n      -6px 0 14px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35),\n      inset 1px 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);\n    transform-origin: right center;\n  }\n  /* Closed: a glass tab just inside the frame. */\n  .edge-tab.is-closed {\n    --flip: -90deg;\n    border-left: 0;\n    border-radius: 0 20px 20px 0 / 0 23px 23px 0;\n    transform-origin: left center;\n  }''','''  /* A solid tab on the frame's edge: hanging over the sidebar while it is\n     open, just inside the frame while it is closed. */\n  .edge-tab.is-open,\n  .edge-tab.is-closed {\n    border: 1px solid var(--library-border);\n    background: var(--library-frame);\n  }\n  .edge-tab.is-open {\n    --flip: 90deg;\n    margin-left: -29px;\n    border-right: 0;\n    border-radius: 14px 0 0 14px;\n    box-shadow:\n      -6px 0 14px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35),\n      inset 1px 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);\n    transform-origin: right center;\n  }\n  .edge-tab.is-closed {\n    --flip: -90deg;\n    border-left: 0;\n    border-radius: 0 14px 14px 0;\n    box-shadow:\n      6px 0 14px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35),\n      inset -1px 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);\n    transform-origin: left center;\n  }''')\nio.open(p,'w',encoding='utf8',newline='').write(s)\nEOF\npython /tmp/edit3.py && bunx biome check --write src/App.tsx src/App.css src/components/Tooltip src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx src/ReaderView.tsx src/components/OpenSourceLicenses 2>&1 | tail -15; bunx tsc-rs --noEmit 2>&1 | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
