{"parentUuid":"b184ca10-88e0-4a2a-afda-def1a716221e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f7d7ab50-f167-4ae0-a78a-a910caf14c46","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, Bash, Edit, Grep, PowerShell, Read, SendMessage, TaskStop, ToolSearch, WebFetch, WebSearch, Write, mcp__col__get_component, mcp__col__get_library, mcp__col__search_components, mcp__col__search_libraries, mcp__paper__find_nodes, mcp__paper__get_guide, mcp__paper__get_screenshot, mcp__paper__get_tree_summary, mcp__paper__open_file, mcp__t3-code__delegate_task, mcp__t3-code__html_preview, mcp__t3-code__html_render, mcp__t3-code__link_pull_request, mcp__t3-code__orchestrator_capabilities, mcp__t3-code__preview_click, mcp__t3-code__preview_evaluate, mcp__t3-code__preview_open, mcp__t3-code__preview_resize, mcp__t3-code__preview_snapshot, mcp__t3-code__preview_status, mcp__t3-code__task_status</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Branch and PR:** all work is on branch `feat/glass-surface`, PR #170.\n     - Standing instruction: \"commit and push to 170 when your done just not to 174 yet\".\n     - Rebasing #174 is deferred until the user asks.\n   - **Done and pushed earlier:**\n     - Sidebar overlap animation.\n     - Edge blur.\n     - Grid/list fade.\n     - Toolbar layout: Add moved to the sidebar, view toggle dock at the bottom.\n     - Mascot roaming removed.\n     - Appearance tab with a pill vs segmented view toggle; segmented shows text only.\n   - **Open source licenses page:** done in commit `18bbf3d`.\n   - **Col review:** \"go look though all the good libraries and components in col…\". I answered with recommendations.\n     - The user plans a big Tailwind rewrite with a component system using Base UI later (\"just not yet\").\n     - The user wanted the right-click menu now; it was done in `0b0cac5`.\n     - The count-up already existed (#167). I added its missing React Bits credit.\n   - **Previous request:** \"turn off autohide on the gradual blur and also make the library cards by default fill up to the blue line but be able to scroll downwards to where they by default sit now… same for list view too. also fix this thumbnail bug\". Follow-up: \"the sidebar close button needs to be level to the mascot and app name and changed in shape… more the general size\". Done in `24252e5`.\n   - **CURRENT request (latest user message):**\n     - \"also I thought you added tooltips? many things like all the controls for spaces, and the grid/list toggle icons dont have tooltips.\"\n     - \"also find a nice filter button from col we can style so that the license page can be filtered by license.\"\n     - \"also the sidebar button is the right size but too round, I liked the rounded corners it had before, and its only a teeny tiny bit too big.\"\n     - \"also when the sidebar is closed and the button shows over the library it turns into liquid glass, I dont like that just keep it like it opqaue like always.\"\n     - \"however the tooltips do need to follow the liquid glass/css glass setting.\"\n     - Context menu: \"get rid of the open option and just leave archive and rename the star to top of mind to favorite, im thinking of something we're gonna do later. and get rid of the line break between the options too\"\n   - **AGENTS.md rules (must keep following):**\n     - Never kill processes found by name/path pattern; kill only the PID captured at spawn.\n     - Never write to the live library.\n     - No hardcoded ports or paths.\n     - No calls home or analytics.\n     - No PRs unless asked.\n     - No repo-wide checks.\n     - Test UI in the real app with screenshots saved to `C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\<task>\\`.\n     - Changelog: one line per entry; trivial UI tweaks skip it.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Stack:** Electron 44 preview, Vite, React 19, plain CSS (not Tailwind), hugeicons.\n   - **Liquid glass:** `LiquidGlass` (WebGPU + HTML-in-Canvas) draws glass under every `.glass` element inside `targetRoots`.\n     - Elements get `data-liquid` once drawn, and their CSS glass is then cleared.\n     - It only refracts the library stage, so it's wrong over the sidebar or the item overlay.\n   - **CSS glass for other places:** `.css-glass` was added as the same CSS surface as `.glass`, but liquid glass never targets it.\n   - **Library scroller:** `VirtuosoMasonry` with className `library-grid` is the scroller inside `.library-scroll`. It remounts on `libraryGridKey`, which is the joined item ids.\n   - **Electron verification workflow:**\n     1. Build with `bunx vite build --mode electron-preview`.\n     2. Create a scratch dir with mktemp; its path goes in /tmp/ink-scratch, holding pid, port and reg.reg.\n     3. Back up the registry: `MSYS2_ARG_CONV_EXCL='*' reg export 'HKCU\\Software\\Classes\\inkling' \"$(cygpath -w $S/reg.reg)\"`.\n     4. Launch `(unset ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE; node_modules/electron/dist/electron.exe . --preview --user-data-dir=\"$(cygpath -w $S/ud)\" --remote-debugging-port=0 > $S/out.log 2>&1 & echo $! > $S/pid)` and read `ud/DevToolsActivePort`.\n     5. Drive it with the CDP scripts in `C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\liquid-glass-run\\`:\n        - `ev.ts <port> '<expr>' [screenshotName]`\n        - `reload.ts`\n        - `ctxmenu.ts`\n        - `licenses.ts`\n     6. Clean up: kill the PID, `reg import`, `rm -rf` the scratch dir.\n   - **Checks:**\n     - `bunx tsc-rs --noEmit`\n     - `bunx biome check --write <files>`\n     - `bunx knip`\n     - `bun test <files>`\n   - **Commit:** `timeout 60 git -c core.hooksPath=/nonexistent commit -q -F -` with a message ending \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\", then `git push -q`.\n   - **Editing:** Python edits must use `io.open(..., newline='')` to keep LF endings; plain open on Windows wrote CRLF. Biome --write fixes endings.\n   - **node_modules:** it was deleted externally mid-session. I reinstalled with `bun install --frozen-lockfile`. Install scripts don't run (no trustedDependencies), so Electron's binary was fetched by hand: `cd node_modules/electron && node install.js`.\n   - **coss ui `packages/ui` is AGPL:** avoid copying it. The kloq package is MIT.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **scripts/third-party-licenses/** — committed in `18bbf3d`.\n     - `collect.mjs` builds the closure of production dependencies and resolves packages the way Node does.\n     - `collect.d.mts`\n     - `collect.test.ts`\n     - `notices.json` — React Bits Count Up entry added in `0b0cac5`, pointing at `src/components/GradualBlur/LICENSE.md`.\n     - `Apache-2.0.txt`\n   - **vite.config.ts** — the `thirdPartyLicenses()` plugin emits `third-party-licenses.json`.\n   - **src/components/OpenSourceLicenses/OpenSourceLicenses.tsx and .css** — the licenses settings page.\n     - Search across name, version and license.\n     - Expandable rows.\n     - `entry.sourceUrl` link, whose `title` is now converted to `data-tooltip`.\n     - ThirdPartyLicense type: `{name, version: string|null, license: string, sourceUrl: string|null, description?, noticeText}`.\n     - The page shows \"N notices\" in `.licenses-toolbar`, next to `.licenses-search`.\n     - **Pending:** add a filter by license.\n   - **src/components/CountUp.tsx** — header comment added crediting React Bits Count Up, with license text in GradualBlur/LICENSE.md.\n   - **src/components/ContextMenu/ContextMenu.tsx and .css** — committed in `0b0cac5`.\n     - `ContextMenu({x,y,label,entries,returnFocus,onClose})` renders through a portal into document.body.\n     - `ContextMenuEntry = {label, icon: IconSvgElement, onSelect} | \"separator\"`.\n     - Flips at the window edges.\n     - Arrow, Home and End keys move focus; Escape and Tab close it and return focus.\n     - Closes on pointerdown outside, wheel, resize and blur.\n     - Separators render as `<hr>`.\n     - CSS reuses the Space menu's surface.\n   - **src/App.tsx — key current state**\n     - **Card menu:** `LibraryCardContext` has `onOpenMenu?`. Cards get `onContextMenu` except in archive selection mode. State is `cardMenu {item, card, x, y}`.\n     - **`cardMenuEntries`, as just edited (uncommitted):**\n       - Open removed; entries starts as `[]`.\n       - Read (if article content).\n       - \"Favorite\"/\"Unfavorite\" calling togglePinItem.\n       - If `sourceUrl` (only http(s): `item.sourceUrl?.match(/^https?:\\/\\//u)`), two entries:\n         - `Open <host>`, which opens the link in a new window.\n         - \"Copy link\", which writes to the clipboard and shows the toast \"Link copied\".\n       - \"Show in folder\" (desktop only).\n       - \"Archive\" calling forgetItem.\n       - All separators removed.\n       - `const { item } = cardMenu;`, and `selectLibraryItem` removed from the deps.\n     - **Rest scroll (committed in `24252e5`):**\n       ```ts\n       const restScrollKey = isSerendipityView ? \"\" : libraryGridKey;\n       useLayoutEffect(() => {\n         const scroll = libraryScrollRef.current;\n         if (!restScrollKey || !scroll) return;\n         const gap = Number.parseFloat(getComputedStyle(scroll).getPropertyValue(\"--library-rest-gap\"));\n         let frame = 0; let tries = 0;\n         const apply = () => {\n           const grid = scroll.querySelector<HTMLElement>(\".library-grid\");\n           if (grid) grid.scrollTop = gap;\n           if ((!grid || grid.scrollTop < gap) && ++tries < 10) frame = requestAnimationFrame(apply);\n         };\n         apply();\n         return () => cancelAnimationFrame(frame);\n       }, [restScrollKey]);\n       ```\n     - **Uncommitted edits:**\n       - `edgeTabRef` replaced with `const tooltipLayerRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);`.\n       - LiquidGlass gets `targetRoots={[captureBarRef, viewDockRef, tooltipLayerRef]}`.\n       - `SidebarEdgeTab({ isOpen, onToggle })` no longer takes a ref.\n       - The tab's className uses `is-closed` without `glass`.\n       - The tab has `data-tooltip={isOpen ? \"Close sidebar\" : \"Open sidebar\"}`.\n       - `<TooltipLayer ref={tooltipLayerRef} />` is rendered before the ContextMenu.\n       - Import added: `import { TooltipLayer } from \"./components/Tooltip/TooltipLayer\";`.\n       - Removed: the `type RefObject` import and the `ViewIcon` import.\n       - 16 `title=` attributes converted to `data-tooltip=`:\n         - Restore to library\n         - archive select/delete\n         - Open reader\n         - Add a Space\n         - Change color\n         - Move Space up and down\n         - Rename Space\n         - Delete Space\n         - Add something to your library (×2)\n         - the update version text\n         - Settings\n         - Clear search\n         - Grid view\n         - List view\n   - **src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx** (uncommitted) — 10 `title=` changed to `data-tooltip=`: Zoom out/in, action.title, the Space options, Star/Unstar, Move to Space, Open host, Show in folder, Archive, Delete permanently.\n   - **src/ReaderView.tsx** (uncommitted) — `title=\"Close reader\"` changed to `data-tooltip`.\n   - **src/components/Tooltip/TooltipLayer.tsx** (new, uncommitted; Biome reformatted it)\n     - One global layer.\n     - Delegated listeners: pointerover/pointerout on `[data-tooltip]` (touch ignored), focusin (`:focus-visible` shows immediately), focusout hides, pointerdown in capture phase hides, Escape, wheel and window blur.\n     - `SHOW_DELAY_MS=500`; `SKIP_DELAY_MS=400` for instant re-show; `GAP=8`; `EDGE=6`.\n     - A MutationObserver updates the text if the anchor's data-tooltip changes.\n     - Placed below the anchor, or above it if there's no room, clamped horizontally. It stays `visibility:hidden` until placed.\n     - `LIQUID_ANCHORS = \".capture-bar, .view-dock\"`.\n     - The class is `tooltip glass` when the anchor is inside that liquid chrome, otherwise `tooltip css-glass`.\n     - Renders `<div ref={ref} className=\"tooltip-layer\" aria-hidden=\"true\">`.\n   - **src/components/Tooltip/Tooltip.css** (new)\n     ```css\n     .tooltip-layer { position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 2000; pointer-events: none; }\n     .tooltip { position: fixed; max-width: 280px; padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 9px; color: var(--library-text); font: 500 12px / 16px var(--font-ui); animation: tooltip-in 0.12s ease-out; }\n     @keyframes tooltip-in { from { opacity: 0; } }\n     ```\n     plus a reduced-motion rule turning the animation off.\n   - **src/App.css**\n     - Uncommitted:\n       - `.glass,\\n.css-glass {` now share the glass surface rule.\n       - Edge tab: top 26px, 30×44.\n       - Open and closed states share `border: 1px solid var(--library-border); background: var(--library-frame)`.\n       - is-open: margin-left -29px, radius `14px 0 0 14px`, left shadow.\n       - is-closed: radius `0 14px 14px 0`, mirrored shadow.\n     - Committed earlier:\n       - `.add-button.is-compact` margin-left 28px.\n       - `--library-rest-gap: 52px` on `.library-scroll`; the grid's padding-top uses it.\n       - `.library-scroll .library-grid > * { min-height: calc(100% + var(--library-rest-gap)); }`.\n       - List-mode thumbnails use `height: 100%; min-height: 155px` for `.card-image-wrap`, `.card-paper-art`, `.post-art` and `.x-post-art`.\n   - **src/components/LibraryEdgeFade.tsx** — committed: `hoverIntensity: 0` removed and the comment updated.\n   - **docs/changelog.md (Unreleased):**\n     - Added: right-click menu (#170); licenses page (#170).\n     - Fixed: list thumbnails (#170).\n     - The right-click line still mentions \"open, read, star…\", so it needs updating for the current changes.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Missing type declarations:** tsc TS7016 for `collect.mjs`. Fixed by adding `collect.d.mts` and importing the type from \"collect.mjs\".\n   - **node_modules disappeared** (not by me). Reinstalled with the frozen lockfile and installed the Electron binary by hand.\n   - **CRLF line endings** from Python edits made Biome flag formatting. Fixed with biome --write; now using `newline=''`.\n   - **`role=\"separator\"` on a div:** Biome flagged it, so it became `<hr>`.\n   - **Context menu label:** `hostnameForUrl` lives in the lazy-loaded overlay, so I inlined the URL parse instead. Demo seed sourceUrls are relative paths, so link entries are limited to http(s).\n   - **Broken regex:** a sed edit mangled it. Fixed with the Edit tool to use `.match(/^https?:\\/\\//u)`.\n   - **Rest scroll stuck at 0:** setting scrollTop in a layout effect didn't stick because Virtuoso sizes its columns later. Fixed with rAF retries (up to 10).\n   - **Biome warnings about extra hook deps:** isSerendipityView, then selectLibraryItem. Fixed with restScrollKey and by removing selectLibraryItem.\n   - **Unused symbols after the latest edits:** TS6133 for `ViewIcon` and `card`. Removed both.\n   - **User corrections:**\n     - The segmented toggle should be text only.\n     - I hadn't actually added tooltips.\n     - The sidebar tab became too round; they want the old 14px corners and slightly smaller.\n     - No liquid glass on the closed tab.\n     - Context menu: remove Open, use \"Favorite\", no separators.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Verified in Electron:\n     - Licenses page: 194 notices; search for \"apache\" gives 12.\n     - Context menu: keyboard navigation, focus return, wheel close, star and archive.\n     - Rest scroll at 52px: card top at 37 in grid, list and short Spaces; scrolling up shows 84.\n     - List thumbnail gaps measure 0.\n     - Edge tab position.\n   - **Latest batch verification:** biome, tsc-rs and knip all came back clean. The last command printed only \"Checked 5 files… No fixes applied\", with no tsc or knip errors.\n   - Known: `@liquid-dom/core` declares no license (flagged to the user).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"go look though all the good libraries and components in col and see if there's anything available that were can use to improve inkling, make it look better, nicer, or more polished\"\n   - \"well I'm going to be doing a huge rewrite over to tailwind and setting up a kind of component system too pretty soon. oh yeah you get it. I was gonna use base ui. just not yet. I do think a right click menu would be nice to add now though. I like tooltips too but what would the small menus look like? also I thought added something like the counting up library total a day or too ago?\"\n   - (with screenshots) \"turn off autohide on the gradual blur and also make the library cards by default fill up to the blue line but be able to scroll downwards to where they by default sit now [Image]. same for list view too. also fix this thumbnail bug [Image]\"\n   - (with screenshot) \"also the sidebar close button needs to be level to the mascot and app name and changed in shape [Image]. my drawing is a little sloopy so thats not the shape I want it but more the general size\"\n   - (with context menu screenshot) \"also I thought you added tooltips? many things like all the controls for spaces, and the grid/list toggle icons dont have tooltips. also find a nice filter button from col we can style so that the license page can be filtered by license. also the sidebar button is the right size but too round, I liked the rounded corners it had before, and its only a teeny tiny bit too big. also when the sidebar is closed and the button shows over the library it turns into liquid glass, I dont like that just keep it like it opqaue like always. however the tooltips do need to follow the liquid glass/css glass setting. [Image] get rid of the open option and just leave archive and rename the star to top of mind to favorite, im thinking of something we're gonna do later. and get rid of the line break between the options too\"\n   - Earlier standing: \"commit and push to 170 when your done just not to 174 yet\".\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **License filter:** find a filter button in Col (use the deferred `mcp__col__*` tools via ToolSearch) and build a styled filter on the licenses page so it can be filtered by license.\n     - Plain CSS, no Tailwind or Base UI dependency.\n     - Avoid AGPL code.\n     - Probably a \"Filter\" button opening a small menu of the distinct license ids with counts, matching the ContextMenu/Space-menu surface, combined with the search.\n   - **Electron check of the current batch:**\n     - Tooltips on Space controls, the grid/list icons and the sidebar tab, with liquid glass on the dock and capture bar and CSS glass elsewhere.\n     - Opaque closed tab with 14px corners at 30×44.\n     - Context menu without Open, with \"Favorite\", no separators.\n     - Take screenshots.\n   - **Changelog:** update the right-click line, which mentions \"star\" and \"open\", and consider a tooltips line.\n   - **Commit and push to #170.**\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was partway through the latest request. Done so far, uncommitted:\n   - The TooltipLayer component and its CSS.\n   - The `.css-glass` class.\n   - `title` swapped for `data-tooltip` across App.tsx, ExpandedItemOverlay, ReaderView and OpenSourceLicenses.\n   - The tooltip layer registered as a LiquidGlass target root, and the edge tab removed from glass.\n   - The edge tab restyled: opaque in both states, 14px radius, 30×44 at top 26px.\n   - The context menu: Open removed, Favorite/Unfavorite, separators gone.\n\n   The last command ran biome, tsc-rs and knip on src/App.tsx, src/components/Tooltip and src/components/ContextMenu with no errors.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   - Build (`bunx vite build --mode electron-preview`) and verify the tooltip, tab and context menu changes in the Electron preview using the scratch-profile workflow, with screenshots.\n   - Then do the remaining piece of the user's request: \"also find a nice filter button from col we can style so that the license page can be filtered by license\". Search Col via ToolSearch for the `mcp__col__search_components` tool, with a query like \"filter\" or \"toggle group\" / \"chip\".\n   - Implement a styled license filter in `OpenSourceLicenses.tsx`.\n   - Update the changelog, commit, and push to #170.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\chris\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"52c6a670-e5e1-4d4b-bf69-3ef8a677896e","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:37:53.536Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":0,"turnIndex":168},"turnOrigin":"sdk","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["256028d5-5f9c-444a-a7f0-c4b6cf276d60"],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"52c6a670-e5e1-4d4b-bf69-3ef8a677896e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304\\src\\components\\Tooltip\\TooltipLayer.tsx","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304\\src\\components\\Tooltip\\TooltipLayer.tsx","content":"import { type RefObject, useEffect, useLayoutEffect, useRef, useState } from \"react\";\nimport \"./Tooltip.css\";\n\n// One tooltip for the whole app. Controls opt in with `data-tooltip=\"…\"` (in\n// place of `title`, whose native tooltip is slow and ignores the theme), and\n// this layer shows it on hover after a beat, or at once on keyboard focus.\n// Moving straight from one control to the next skips the wait.\n\nconst SHOW_DELAY_MS = 500;\n// Within this long of one tooltip closing, the next opens without the delay.\nconst SKIP_DELAY_MS = 400;\nconst GAP = 8;\nconst EDGE = 6;\n// Anchors in this chrome sit over the library stage, where liquid glass can\n// draw the tooltip (LiquidGlass.tsx). Anywhere else the stage is not behind\n// it, so it keeps the CSS glass.\nconst LIQUID_ANCHORS = \".capture-bar, .view-dock\";\n\ntype Tip = { anchor: HTMLElement; text: string };\n\nexport function TooltipLayer({ ref }: { ref: RefObject<HTMLDivElement | null> }) {\n  const [tip, setTip] = useState<Tip | null>(null);\n  const tipRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);\n  const [placement, setPlacement] = useState<{ left: number; top: number } | null>(null);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    let timer = 0;\n    let closedAt = 0;\n    let current: HTMLElement | null = null;\n    const show = (anchor: HTMLElement, immediate: boolean) => {\n      const text = anchor.dataset.tooltip;\n      if (!text) return;\n      current = anchor;\n      window.clearTimeout(timer);\n      const open = () => setTip({ anchor, text });\n      if (immediate || performance.now() - closedAt < SKIP_DELAY_MS) open();\n      else timer = window.setTimeout(open, SHOW_DELAY_MS);\n    };\n    const hide = () => {\n      window.clearTimeout(timer);\n      if (current) closedAt = performance.now();\n      current = null;\n      setTip(null);\n    };\n    const anchorOf = (target: EventTarget | null) =>\n      target instanceof Element ? target.closest<HTMLElement>(\"[data-tooltip]\") : null;\n\n    const onOver = (event: PointerEvent) => {\n      if (event.pointerType === \"touch\") return;\n      const anchor = anchorOf(event.target);\n      if (anchor === current) return;\n      if (current) hide();\n      if (anchor) show(anchor, false);\n    };\n    const onOut = (event: PointerEvent) => {\n      if (!current) return;\n      const next = event.relatedTarget;\n      if (next instanceof Node && current.contains(next)) return;\n      hide();\n    };\n    const onFocus = (event: FocusEvent) => {\n      const anchor = anchorOf(event.target);\n      if (anchor && anchor === event.target && anchor.matches(\":focus-visible\")) show(anchor, true);\n    };\n    const onKey = (event: KeyboardEvent) => {\n      if (event.key === \"Escape\") hide();\n    };\n\n    document.addEventListener(\"pointerover\", onOver);\n    document.addEventListener(\"pointerout\", onOut);\n    document.addEventListener(\"focusin\", onFocus);\n    document.addEventListener(\"focusout\", hide);\n    document.addEventListener(\"pointerdown\", hide, true);\n    document.addEventListener(\"keydown\", onKey, true);\n    window.addEventListener(\"wheel\", hide, { capture: true, passive: true });\n    window.addEventListener(\"blur\", hide);\n    return () => {\n      window.clearTimeout(timer);\n      document.removeEventListener(\"pointerover\", onOver);\n      document.removeEventListener(\"pointerout\", onOut);\n      document.removeEventListener(\"focusin\", onFocus);\n      document.removeEventListener(\"focusout\", hide);\n      document.removeEventListener(\"pointerdown\", hide, true);\n      document.removeEventListener(\"keydown\", onKey, true);\n      window.removeEventListener(\"wheel\", hide, true);\n      window.removeEventListener(\"blur\", hide);\n    };\n  }, []);\n\n  // A control whose label changes while hovered (Star → Unstar) updates in place.\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (!tip) return;\n    const observer = new MutationObserver(() => {\n      const text = tip.anchor.dataset.tooltip;\n      if (!text || !tip.anchor.isConnected) setTip(null);\n      else if (text !== tip.text) setTip({ ...tip, text });\n    });\n    observer.observe(tip.anchor, { attributes: true, attributeFilter: [\"data-tooltip\"] });\n    return () => observer.disconnect();\n  }, [tip]);\n\n  // Below the control, or above it when there is no room (the view dock).\n  useLayoutEffect(() => {\n    const element = tipRef.current;\n    if (!tip || !element) {\n      setPlacement(null);\n      return;\n    }\n    const anchor = tip.anchor.getBoundingClientRect();\n    const { width, height } = element.getBoundingClientRect();\n    const below = anchor.bottom + GAP;\n    const top = below + height > window.innerHeight - EDGE ? anchor.top - GAP - height : below;\n    const left = Math.min(\n      Math.max(EDGE, anchor.left + anchor.width / 2 - width / 2),\n      window.innerWidth - EDGE - width,\n    );\n    setPlacement({ left, top });\n  }, [tip]);\n\n  const liquid = tip?.anchor.closest(LIQUID_ANCHORS) != null;\n  return (\n    <div ref={ref} className=\"tooltip-layer\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n      {tip && (\n        <div\n          ref={tipRef}\n          className={`tooltip ${liquid ? \"glass\" : \"css-glass\"}`}\n          style={placement ?? { visibility: \"hidden\" }}\n        >\n          {tip.text}\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n","numLines":135,"startLine":1,"totalLines":135}},"displayPath":"src\\components\\Tooltip\\TooltipLayer.tsx"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e7a97a6a-10f3-4836-8000-d69ac4e87a43","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:37:53.742Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read too