{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"33b385003532f18f84d12d2b133184b0f1799d39244787ef64bd4dcfaacb741c","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm planning a faceted \"License\" filter styled like the shadcn Tasks example, built in plain CSS with a dashed button, plus-circle icon, selected-value badges, and a popover checkbox list showing license counts and a clear-filters option, keeping it simple without an internal search since there are only about 10 licenses.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll recreate shadcn's faceted filter pattern—a dashed \"+ License\" button with a checklist showing counts per license—using plain CSS. Let me read through the page first.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014DHCw38176m6eiqFECToFz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && cat src/components/OpenSourceLicenses/OpenSourceLicenses.tsx; cat src/components/OpenSourceLicenses/OpenSourceLicenses.css"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
