{"parentUuid":"bfd7b32b-dbad-4078-92f3-0bff1dfaba9d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_014DHCw38176m6eiqFECToFz","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c33d87a5-9768-40a3-ad95-294d21bc4a70","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:38:47.130Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"c33d87a5-9768-40a3-ad95-294d21bc4a70","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFww6RNTvnPXnxUhhBpy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need a separate LicenseFilter component with its own popover since ContextMenu closes on selection, which won't work for checkboxes that need to stay open while toggling. I'm thinking through whether it needs a portal, since the toolbar sits outside the settings scroller but the settings panel itself might clip with overflow hidden.\n\nI decide the popover is short enough that it should fit without overflow issues. Compound license expressions like \"(MIT OR Apache-2.0)\" count as distinct values, and the toolbar layout has the count on the left, filter button and search on the right, with the count text switching to \"N of M notices\" when filtered.\n\nNow I'm writing the state hooks for license filtering, a memoized count-by-license map sorted descending, and the filtering logic that checks selected licenses plus search text. Writing the LicenseFilter component with open state, a ref for outside-click detection, and dismiss handlers for pointer events and Escape key...\n\nI continue defining keyboard navigation for the options list, with each item rendered as a checkable menu item showing a checkbox, license name, and count, plus a \"Clear filter\" footer when selections exist. I'm also deciding on button contents—an icon, \"License\" label, and badges for selected items—and need to verify the exact icon names exist in the hugeicons library.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4134,"cache_read_input_tokens":68813,"output_tokens":977,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":752},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":413