{"parentUuid":"08d9013f-0745-444b-9f17-a6dc65fb5d5e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f7d7ab50-f167-4ae0-a78a-a910caf14c46","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JYRzy31azjbkLE5RpGb1xJ","type":"tool_result","content":"The operation completed successfully.\r\r\n31:- Right-click a card to open, read, star, open its link, copy its link, show it in its folder, or archive it (#170)\n32:- Settings → General → Open source licenses lists every shipped dependency, vendored component, and bundled model with its license text and source (#170)\n33:- Settings → Appearance switches components between alternative looks while we compare them, starting with the grid/list toggle as the current pill or a coss ui segmented control (#170)\n72:- Liquid glass in the desktop app: the library toolbar, search chip, collapsed sidebar tab and image zoom control refract what is behind them through WebGPU and Chromium's HTML-in-Canvas, and fall back to the CSS glass when either is unavailable (#170)\n76:- List view thumbnails fill rows that grow taller than the artwork, instead of leaving a strip at the bottom (#170)\n85:- Library cards load remote images in CORS mode and the desktop app adds a CORS header to image responses, so the liquid glass canvas can draw them; no extra requests are made (#170)\n86:- Switching between grid and list fades the cards out and pops the new view in, list rows top to bottom and grid cards from the top left, instead of morphing each card between layouts (#170)\n87:- Add moves to the foot of the sidebar, with a round + in the toolbar while the sidebar is closed, and the grid/list toggle floats at the bottom centre of the library. The back and forward buttons are gone; the mouse side buttons and Alt+Left/Right still step through history (#170)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b9cd4177-1855-47a4-ae58-547e23b48fab","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:43:32.891Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"The operation completed successfully.\r\r\n31:- Right-click a card to open, read, star, open its link, copy its link, show it in its folder, or archive it (#170)\n32:- Settings → General → Open source licenses lists every shipped dependency, vendored component, and bundled model with its license text and source (#170)\n33:- Settings → Appearance switches components between alternative looks while we compare them, starting with the grid/list toggle as the current pill or a coss ui segmented control (#170)\n72:- Liquid glass in the desktop app: the library toolbar, search chip, collapsed sidebar tab and image zoom control refract what is behind them through WebGPU and Chromium's HTML-in-Canvas, and fall back to the CSS glass when either is unavailable (#170)\n76:- List view thumbnails fill rows that grow taller than the artwork, instead of leaving a strip at the bottom (#170)\n85:- Library cards load remote images in CORS mode and the desktop app adds a CORS header to image responses, so the liquid glass canvas can draw them; no extra requests are made (#170)\n86:- Switching between grid and list fades the cards out and pops the new view in, list rows top to bottom and grid cards from the top left, instead of morphing each card between layouts (#170)\n87:- Add moves to the foot of the sidebar, with a round + in the toolbar while the sidebar is closed, and the grid/list toggle floats at the bottom centre of the library. The back and forward buttons are gone; the mouse side buttons and Alt+Left/Right still step through history (#170)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"08d9013f-0745-444b-9f17-a6dc65fb5d5e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
