{"parentUuid":"b467866f-586d-4a0a-8048-13a29ca604dc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFxPK7aVvfFx2BQSNvkV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm noting the overlay sits as a fixed layer above the frame, inset by padding, which is why the library chrome peeks through at the edges since that padding area stays uncovered. The blue at bottom-left looks like a focus ring on a card, while the bottom-right arrows seem to point toward the inspector action row and a line extending to the window edge.\n\nI'm now thinking the inspector should actually extend all the way to the bottom of the window rather than stopping at the frame's bottom padding — that gap below it is the issue the arrow is flagging. I'm unsure who introduced this workaround originally, maybe from an earlier commit opening items into a full-frame stage, but regardless it needs fixing by having the item view properly replace the library content as a real screen within the main frame rather than just overlaying it.\n\nLooking more closely at the screenshots, the edge tab that toggles the sidebar overlaps the top-left corner of the item overlay since the overlay starts flush with the frame's padded edge, while in the normal library view the grid starts lower and avoids the tab entirely. The real fix is to render the item view inline within main-content, hiding the library's chrome while it's open, and still deriving the flight animation's destination rect from the item view's own placeholder element — this is a bigger refactor than I first thought, so I want to inspect the screens more precisely before proceeding.\n\nActually, with the window bottom at 748 and the line at 715, the gap from 717 to 748 looks like leftover frame padding — if the inspector extended to the real window edge that space would disappear. I should build and launch the preview, open an item, and take a screenshot to check the actual main-content CSS behavior.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3926,"cache_read_input_tokens":116197,"output_tokens":1447,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1263},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3926,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1447,"cache_read_input_tokens":116197,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3926,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3926},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":15547,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFxPJj2No5eLyjHbF572","requestRef":"eb1147e7-bfe8-4665-b192-e88dd5894b34","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3e402316-10ce-409b-be09-b1818834f644","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:44:45.826Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
