{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","prNumber":170,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Squidys-Tools/inkling/pull/170","prRepository":"Squidys-Tools/inkling","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:45:13.080Z"}
{"parentUuid":"72d59e8b-f30d-49e7-b324-d75caa9b26f3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFxSYc2KHSpCx2Ezrr2v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm noticing several layout issues: the edge tab overlapping the stage corner, the selected card's blue focus outline peeking out, and the view dock showing at the bottom with a gap below the inspector. The real fix is to render the item view directly as the content of main-content rather than overlaying it.\n\nFor this, the library stage should stay mounted but hidden (visibility/inert) while the item view is open, preserving scroll and card positions for the close flight — since the close animation needs card rects, so the library must become visible again right as that flight starts. I'm restructuring the overlay to be an absolutely-positioned child within main-content instead of a fixed, separately-measured layer, which removes the need for frame rect measuring and the ResizeObserver since the destination simply becomes \"fill the main frame,\" letting the frame's own border-radius clip it naturally. Then I'm laying out the stage on the left with a fixed 320px inspector panel on the right.\n\nBoth panels need to span the full height of main-content, with the inspector getting extra top padding to clear the titlebar/window-controls band, while the stage panel keeps its own inset margins to mimic the original rounded dotted-background panel seen in the library view — effectively becoming a standalone screen without the library's capture bar or dock.\n\nLooking at the user's drawn line, I realize they want the inspector's footer action row bottom-aligned with the stage's bottom edge, meaning I should shift the actions row down so it matches the stage bottom rather than floating higher. I'll also check whether the stage bottom inset should match the left inset (14px) for visual symmetry, since currently the bottom padding looks like it was borrowed from a different region of the library layout.\n\nNow I need to figure out how the expanded overlay sits relative to the edge tab, since the tab's position (top 26, left 0, z-index 32) can collide with the stage's top-left corner when the sidebar is closed — I'll need an inset on the stage so it clears the tab the same way the library's compact add button does.\n\nOther option: inset the stage's left edge when the sidebar is closed so the tab doesn't collide, though that wastes space at the top. Checking the library grid's layout, the cards already start below the tab's vertical band, so that pattern works there, but it's less clear how to apply the same fix to the item view's stage — I might need to just ask instead of guessing further.\n\nActually, I'm reconsidering whether the tab even overlaps the library itself—the capture bar at top is centered, so that's fine. The main-content padding already transitions automatically when the sidebar toggles, and the item view follows suit. I need the library chrome—capture bar, view dock, library scroll—hidden once an item is fully settled open, but visible during the fly-in/fly-out transitions since the card animates from/to the grid; this means the has-open-item class, which spans the entire selection lifecycle, needs to distinguish between flight and settled states.\n\nThe onClose action likely fires at the end of the close flight, so selectedItem remains set throughout—meaning I need a separate \"settled\" signal passed from the overlay up to the App. One approach: make the overlay's background fully opaque and positioned above the capture bar and view dock once settled, so nothing bleeds through and the library naturally shows around the flying card during transitions; this also handles inert/focus behavior since the opaque layer blocks the library's focus outlines. But I'm realizing the current overlay still leaves gaps because it's positioned at the frame rect inset by padding rather than covering the full main area.\n\nThe real fix is to settle the overlay to match main's entire bounding box, letting the inner layout handle its own padding for the stage and inspector, with main's overflow and border radius handling the clipping. This raises a coordinate problem though—since the flight layer is fixed to the viewport and the card's starting rect is in viewport coordinates, I need to convert the destination to main's border-box rect while keeping the positioning math consistent with how the layer sits relative to the app shell's z-index stack.\n\nThe real fix needs to make the underlying library actually inert once settled — not just visually covered but unreachable by keyboard/focus and hidden from rendering, since that's what \"actually doing it\" requires structurally. I'll have the overlay cover the full frame, then once settled, apply `inert` and hide visibility on the library stage behind it.\n\nRather than needing a settled callback from the flight animation, I can simplify: just tie the `inert` attribute to whether `selectedItem` is set, applying it to the library region (capture bar, scroll, dock). This gets the focus/accessibility isolation without extra machinery, while the opaque overlay handles covering visibility during the transition.\n\nI'm weighing whether the overlay should live inside main's DOM for natural focus order and clipping, but the flight coordinates and z-index relative to the edge tab make a fixed position safer — main doesn't create its own stacking context, so keeping things fixed avoids complications. The edge tab sits above the overlay in z-order, which should be fine given the stage's left inset when the sidebar is closed.\n\nThe edge tab staying usable during the sidebar transition works since the ResizeObserver fires continuously as main's width animates. Focus mode and mobile layouts don't need special handling here since they're unaffected or already generic. Now I want to look at the interior layout CSS for the item stage, inspector, and footer actions.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2648,"cache_read_input_tokens":125492,"output_tokens":4375,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4230},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2648,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4375,"cache_read_input_tokens":125492,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2648,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2648},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":49940,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFxSWwKLxmgVhE5d5jAf","requestRef":"ceeabe6a-f172-4bc8-a1e6-91b940ac5ba9","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"18b267d9-d771-41a8-ab74-79c9e9674ecd","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:46:03.990Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"18b267d9-d771-41a8-ab74-79c9e9674ecd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFxSYc2KHSpCx2Ezrr2v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found it: the item view overlay only covers the inner grid area, not the frame's padding, so the sidebar tab, focus ring, dock, and inspector band still peek through. Now checking how the stage and inspector are laid out inside it.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2648,"cache_read_input_tokens":125492,"output_tokens":4375,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4230},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2648,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4375,"cache_read_input_tokens":125492,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2648,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2648},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgFxSWwKLxmgVhE5d5jAf","requestRef":"ceeabe6a-f172-4bc8-a1e6-91b940ac5ba9","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"608d142a-dc27-4132-a01c-33f4b8c06509","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:46:03.998Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"608d142a-dc27-4132-a01c-33f4b8c06509","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFxSYc2KHSpCx2Ezrr2v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018UGjh3CJ5ttXx3RU9rjg3x","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 5296,5420p src/App.css; grep -n \"^\\.item-inspector[a-z-]* {\\|^\\.item-actions\\|^\\.item-inspector-footer\" src/App.css"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2648,"cache_read_input_tokens":125492,"output_tokens":4375,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4230},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2648,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4375,"cache_read_input_tokens":125492,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2648,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2648},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018UGjh3CJ5ttXx3RU9rjg3x":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && sed -n 5296,5420p src/App.css; grep -n \"^\\.item-inspector[a-z-]* {\\|^\\.item-actions\\|^\\.item-inspector-footer\" src/App.css"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_018UGjh3CJ5ttXx3RU9rjg3x":{"cwd":"/c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgFxSWwKLxmgVhE5d5jAf","requestRef":"ceeabe6a-f172-4bc8-a1e6-91b940ac5ba9","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0ad4d967-9653-4374-a8ec-f644d92193d6","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:46:03.999Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"0ad4d967-9653-4374-a8ec-f644d92193d6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fecd25ef-3a39-4b84-8576-5e7ad975e900","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018UGjh3CJ5ttXx3RU9rjg3x","type":"tool_result","content":"}\n/* Paper's frame has no border of its own. A border here would offset the stage\n   and inspector by a pixel, so the viewer and inspector insets would not match. */\n.expanded-overlay {\n  position: absolute;\n  left: 0;\n  top: 0;\n  width: 0;\n  height: 0;\n  overflow: hidden;\n  border-radius: var(--frame-radius) 0 0 var(--frame-radius);\n  background: var(--library-frame);\n  pointer-events: auto;\n}\n.expanded-overlay.is-flying {\n  will-change: left, top, width, height, opacity;\n}\n.item-stage {\n  position: absolute;\n  inset: 0 320px 0 0;\n  display: grid;\n  place-items: center;\n  padding: 72px 40px 72px;\n  overflow: hidden;\n  border: 1px solid var(--library-border);\n  border-radius: 20px;\n  --item-stage-surface:\n    radial-gradient(circle, #2a2623 1px, transparent 1.2px) 0 0 / 18px 18px #121110;\n  background: var(--item-stage-surface);\n  transition:\n    inset 0.32s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1),\n    padding 0.32s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1),\n    border-radius 0.32s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1);\n}\n.expanded-overlay.is-flying .item-stage {\n  inset: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n  border-color: transparent;\n  border-radius: inherit;\n}\n.item-stage-image {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: 50%;\n  left: 50%;\n  display: block;\n  max-width: 100%;\n  max-height: 100%;\n  translate: -50% -50%;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n  box-shadow: 0 24px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);\n}\n.expanded-overlay.is-flying .item-stage-image {\n  box-shadow: none;\n}\n.item-stage-art {\n  width: min(100%, 720px);\n  height: min(100%, 520px);\n  overflow: hidden;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n}\n.item-stage-art > *,\n.item-stage-art .detail-art,\n.item-stage-art .post-art {\n  height: 100%;\n  min-height: 0;\n  margin: 0;\n  border-radius: 0;\n}\n.expanded-overlay.is-flying .item-stage-art {\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 100%;\n  border-radius: 0;\n}\n.item-inspector {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: 0;\n  right: 0;\n  bottom: 0;\n  width: 320px;\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  padding: 6px 16px 4px 18px;\n  font-family: var(--font-body);\n  transition:\n    opacity 0.25s ease 0.08s,\n    translate 0.32s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1);\n}\n.expanded-overlay.is-flying .item-inspector {\n  opacity: 0;\n  translate: 24px 0;\n  pointer-events: none;\n  transition: none;\n}\n.item-inspector-header {\n  display: flex;\n  flex: 0 0 auto;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  height: 40px;\n}\n.item-inspector-tabs {\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 18px;\n}\n.item-inspector-tab {\n  padding: 0;\n  border: 0;\n  background: none;\n  color: var(--library-muted);\n  cursor: pointer;\n  font: 14px / 18px var(--font-body);\n}\n.item-inspector-tab:hover {\n  color: var(--library-text-soft);\n}\n.item-inspector-tab[aria-selected=\"true\"] {\n  color: var(--library-text);\n  font-weight: 600;\n}\n.item-close {\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 6px;\n  margin-left: auto;\n5369:.item-inspector {\n5389:.item-inspector-header {\n5396:.item-inspector-tabs {\n5401:.item-inspector-tab {\n5438:.item-inspector-body {\n5572:.item-actions {\n5577:.item-actions button {\n5590:.item-actions button:hover:not(:disabled) {\n5594:.item-actions button:disabled {","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"45a5cccf-5ca6-402d-bc3a-24c9f1bf7f21","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:46:04.324Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"}\n/* Paper's frame has no border of its own. A border here would offset the stage\n   and inspector by a pixel, so the viewer and inspector insets would not match. */\n.expanded-overlay {\n  position: absolute;\n  left: 0;\n  top: 0;\n  width: 0;\n  height: 0;\n  overflow: hidden;\n  border-radius: var(--frame-radius) 0 0 var(--frame-radius);\n  background: var(--library-frame);\n  pointer-events: auto;\n}\n.expanded-overlay.is-flying {\n  will-change: left, top, width, height, opacity;\n}\n.item-stage {\n  position: absolute;\n  inset: 0 320px 0 0;\n  display: grid;\n  place-items: center;\n  padding: 72px 40px 72px;\n  overflow: hidden;\n  border: 1px solid var(--library-border);\n  border-radius: 20px;\n  --item-stage-surface:\n    radial-gradient(circle, #2a2623 1px, transparent 1.2px) 0 0 / 18px 18px #121110;\n  background: var(--item-stage-surface);\n  transition:\n    inset 0.32s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1),\n    padding 0.32s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1),\n    border-radius 0.32s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1);\n}\n.expanded-overlay.is-flying .item-stage {\n  inset: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n  border-color: transparent;\n  border-radius: inherit;\n}\n.item-stage-image {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: 50%;\n  left: 50%;\n  display: block;\n  max-width: 100%;\n  max-height: 100%;\n  translate: -50% -50%;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n  box-shadow: 0 24px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);\n}\n.expanded-overlay.is-flying .item-stage-image {\n  box-shadow: none;\n}\n.item-stage-art {\n  width: min(100%, 720px);\n  height: min(100%, 520px);\n  overflow: hidden;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n}\n.item-stage-art > *,\n.item-stage-art .detail-art,\n.item-stage-art .post-art {\n  height: 100%;\n  min-height: 0;\n  margin: 0;\n  border-radius: 0;\n}\n.expanded-overlay.is-flying .item-stage-art {\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 100%;\n  border-radius: 0;\n}\n.item-inspector {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: 0;\n  right: 0;\n  bottom: 0;\n  width: 320px;\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  padding: 6px 16px 4px 18px;\n  font-family: var(--font-body);\n  transition:\n    opacity 0.25s ease 0.08s,\n    translate 0.32s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1);\n}\n.expanded-overlay.is-flying .item-inspector {\n  opacity: 0;\n  translate: 24px 0;\n  pointer-events: none;\n  transition: none;\n}\n.item-inspector-header {\n  display: flex;\n  flex: 0 0 auto;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  height: 40px;\n}\n.item-inspector-tabs {\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 18px;\n}\n.item-inspector-tab {\n  padding: 0;\n  border: 0;\n  background: none;\n  color: var(--library-muted);\n  cursor: pointer;\n  font: 14px / 18px var(--font-body);\n}\n.item-inspector-tab:hover {\n  color: var(--library-text-soft);\n}\n.item-inspector-tab[aria-selected=\"true\"] {\n  color: var(--library-text);\n  font-weight: 600;\n}\n.item-close {\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 6px;\n  margin-left: auto;\n5369:.item-inspector {\n5389:.item-inspector-header {\n5396:.item-inspector-tabs {\n5401:.item-inspector-tab {\n5438:.item-inspector-body {\n5572:.item-actions {\n5577:.item-actions button {\n5590:.item-actions button:hover:not(:disabled) {\n5594:.item-actions button:disabled {","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0ad4d967-9653-4374-a8ec-f644d92193d6","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"45a5cccf-5ca6-402d-bc3a-24c9f1bf7f21","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14973849 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"19e69798-c75b-4002-9a1c-32b8c36ae236","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:46:04.330Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14973849 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"00a1130805ecd20848387e890f8891ae4acf6dcbb62220b2bd47d88f253433c0","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm noticing several layout issues: the edge tab overlapping the stage corner, the selected card's blue focus outline peeking out, and the view dock showing at the bottom with a gap below the inspector. The real fix is to render the item view directly as the content of main-content rather than overlaying it.\n\nFor this, the library stage should stay mounted but hidden (visibility/inert) while the item view is open, preserving scroll and card positions for the close flight — since the close animation needs card rects, so the library must become visible again right as that flight starts. I'm restructuring the overlay to be an absolutely-positioned child within main-content instead of a fixed, separately-measured layer, which removes the need for frame rect measuring and the ResizeObserver since the destination simply becomes \"fill the main frame,\" letting the frame's own border-radius clip it naturally. Then I'm laying out the stage on the left with a fixed 320px inspector panel on the right.\n\nBoth panels need to span the full height of main-content, with the inspector getting extra top padding to clear the titlebar/window-controls band, while the stage panel keeps its own inset margins to mimic the original rounded dotted-background panel seen in the library view — effectively becoming a standalone screen without the library's capture bar or dock.\n\nLooking at the user's drawn line, I realize they want the inspector's footer action row bottom-aligned with the stage's bottom edge, meaning I should shift the actions row down so it matches the stage bottom rather than floating higher. I'll also check whether the stage bottom inset should match the left inset (14px) for visual symmetry, since currently the bottom padding looks like it was borrowed from a different region of the library layout.\n\nNow I need to figure out how the expanded overlay sits relative to the edge tab, since the tab's position (top 26, left 0, z-index 32) can collide with the stage's top-left corner when the sidebar is closed — I'll need an inset on the stage so it clears the tab the same way the library's compact add button does.\n\nOther option: inset the stage's left edge when the sidebar is closed so the tab doesn't collide, though that wastes space at the top. Checking the library grid's layout, the cards already start below the tab's vertical band, so that pattern works there, but it's less clear how to apply the same fix to the item view's stage — I might need to just ask instead of guessing further.\n\nActually, I'm reconsidering whether the tab even overlaps the library itself—the capture bar at top is centered, so that's fine. The main-content padding already transitions automatically when the sidebar toggles, and the item view follows suit. I need the library chrome—capture bar, view dock, library scroll—hidden once an item is fully settled open, but visible during the fly-in/fly-out transitions since the card animates from/to the grid; this means the has-open-item class, which spans the entire selection lifecycle, needs to distinguish between flight and settled states.\n\nThe onClose action likely fires at the end of the close flight, so selectedItem remains set throughout—meaning I need a separate \"settled\" signal passed from the overlay up to the App. One approach: make the overlay's background fully opaque and positioned above the capture bar and view dock once settled, so nothing bleeds through and the library naturally shows around the flying card during transitions; this also handles inert/focus behavior since the opaque layer blocks the library's focus outlines. But I'm realizing the current overlay still leaves gaps because it's positioned at the frame rect inset by padding rather than covering the full main area.\n\nThe real fix is to settle the overlay to match main's entire bounding box, letting the inner layout handle its own padding for the stage and inspector, with main's overflow and border radius handling the clipping. This raises a coordinate problem though—since the flight layer is fixed to the viewport and the card's starting rect is in viewport coordinates, I need to convert the destination to main's border-box rect while keeping the positioning math consistent with how the layer sits relative to the app shell's z-index stack.\n\nThe real fix needs to make the underlying library actually inert once settled — not just visually covered but unreachable by keyboard/focus and hidden from rendering, since that's what \"actually doing it\" requires structurally. I'll have the overlay cover the full frame, then once settled, apply `inert` and hide visibility on the library stage behind it.\n\nRather than needing a settled callback from the flight animation, I can simplify: just tie the `inert` attribute to whether `selectedItem` is set, applying it to the library region (capture bar, scroll, dock). This gets the focus/accessibility isolation without extra machinery, while the opaque overlay handles covering visibility during the transition.\n\nI'm weighing whether the overlay should live inside main's DOM for natural focus order and clipping, but the flight coordinates and z-index relative to the edge tab make a fixed position safer — main doesn't create its own stacking context, so keeping things fixed avoids complications. The edge tab sits above the overlay in z-order, which should be fine given the stage's left inset when the sidebar is closed.\n\nThe edge tab staying usable during the sidebar transition works since the ResizeObserver fires continuously as main's width animates. Focus mode and mobile layouts don't need special handling here since they're unaffected or already generic. Now I want to look at the interior layout CSS for the item stage, inspector, and footer actions.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found it: the item view overlay only covers the inner grid area, not the frame's padding, so the sidebar tab, focus ring, dock, and inspector band still peek through. Now checking how the stage and inspector are laid out inside it.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018UGjh3CJ5ttXx3RU9rjg3x","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && sed -n 5296,5420p src/App.css; grep -n \"^\\.item-inspector[a-z-]* {\\|^\\.item-actions\\|^\\.item-inspector-footer\" src/App.css"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
