{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"92a78a72f049a6ea9919668d3db0561ea6b2d847961b242a9b447cb64b84d16e","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm checking the z-index layering for GradualBlur and the LiquidGlass canvas relative to other elements, and it looks fine since earlier screenshots show no overlay bleed. Now I'll move on to implementation.\n\nFirst, I'm updating the frameRect calculation in ExpandedItemOverlay to use the frame's padding box rather than its border box, accounting for clientLeft/clientTop offsets. I'm also noting the border radius on the overlay should be one pixel less than the frame radius to sit correctly inside it, then starting to write the CSS for positioning the expanded stage within the frame.\n\nWorking out inset values...\n\nI decide to just go with 13px as a literal value with a comment explaining it's the frame's padding minus its border, accepting the minor mobile offset. I consider whether the overlay should match the frame's border styling but reject it since a border would show during flight animations and the frame itself has none — so I'll keep the overlay on the padding box instead.\n\nWriting stage CSS...\n\nNow I'm figuring out the left inset when the sidebar is closed on desktop: the overlay needs to clear the sidebar tab, which spans from 0 to 30px, plus a gap matching the spacing used elsewhere (about 14px), landing on roughly 43-44px total.\n\nI'm also checking that the stage inset transitions smoothly whenever the sidebar toggles, since both the stage and overlay have their own animated width/inset values tied to a ResizeObserver, and confirming the DOM order so the sibling selector targeting `.sidebar:not(.is-open)` actually applies correctly to the overlay and main content.\n\nNow I'm adjusting the inspector panel's top/bottom insets to align with the new stage boundaries, shifting its header position to sit flush at the correct offset, and checking the actions panel styling to make sure it bottom-aligns with the stage bottom as intended.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Next, the inspector footer's layout and any narrow-window overrides:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QE9kvc5x1YNQeHnCHSvmB3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && sed -n 5560,5600p src/App.css; grep -n \"expanded-overlay\\b\\|\\.item-stage {\\|\\.item-inspector {\" src/App.css | awk -F: '$1<3700 || $1>5600'"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
