{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","id":"ecf948ae-432f-40f8-b299-fd94d4c1ec06","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:49:44.525Z","version":"2.1.306","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"7e0880a1db257d47c14205e44ebf1a3a6a180182c2e0fc44a51d1c78eadb8ea1","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"3eea3491-75e0-4676-a009-7e1bf7f0e295","keep":233,"tail":["ac2624bed7420edf4a1b703d8d15088e4ad2ba305562f4455f915ef33c613431","d57a675d4d1fee544969161f1b0a7fa66f04c944af159acf5b421393355f0cbc","ee5fcda2a9e3534ebc6189ab7436f7ee14d2126e2314c8daca1e4aa0563136c2"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",235,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"b5844c772f14d40c7760bba606fb4c178b3b5171c1675f1921b0cc0f8d3e6784"}
{"parentUuid":"7e115c25-ce74-4c23-9043-682364a46428","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFxnXx9az3zU7pkZqTTX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I realize the padding transition from 72→0 was already present before my change, so my added inset values compound that jumpiness, making the card look like it shrinks then grows at flight start. The fix is to prevent the stage from transitioning into the flying state and only transition out of it.\n\nBut that raises another issue: close flight currently relies on this outward transition to look smooth, so disabling the entry transition could break the close animation differently, and I need to check whether the element renders once without is-flying before a layout effect applies it, since that would explain why the computed style starts mid-transition from settled values.\n\nThe actual trigger is a forced reflow — something in a layout effect calls getBoundingClientRect to measure the frame/card rects, which forces a style recalc and lets the browser interpolate a transition that shouldn't exist. The minimal fix is scoping transition: none to just the open flight using a data attribute like data-flight=\"open\" on the overlay, rather than disabling transitions globally — this bug predates my change but my edits made it more visible, so it's worth fixing now.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2039,"cache_read_input_tokens":161043,"output_tokens":1007,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":862},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2039,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1007,"cache_read_input_tokens":161043,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2039,"cache_c