{"parentUuid":"ced08440-86a8-438d-90a6-178c6a0052f4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFxt1SGpgo5rZjcpDBeK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I should flag that moving the modals is a substantial part of the diff, then wrap up with the final reply.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1082,"cache_read_input_tokens":170612,"output_tokens":842,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":26},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1082,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":842,"cache_read_input_tokens":170612,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1082,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1082},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":6722,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFxt13THWKadE1Kh17mN","requestRef":"b8954678-c437-428b-b7bd-53a3fdba7c40","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"cd4bf338-feab-4779-821b-190f4dbb8817","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:51:06.253Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"cd4bf338-feab-4779-821b-190f4dbb8817","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFxt1SGpgo5rZjcpDBeK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You were right: the item view only pretended to be its own screen. It was a floating layer sized to the card grid's area inside the frame's padding, with the library still live underneath. Everything in that padding showed through: the sidebar tab, the selected card's blue focus ring, the grid/list toggle, and the empty band under the inspector. The two CSS rules that hid the rest were my own patches from earlier in #170. This is fixed and pushed to #170 as `0685f7f`.\n\n**What changed**\n- **It's a real screen now.** An open item takes the whole library frame. The image and the info panel keep clear of the window controls themselves, and the image moves right to clear the sidebar tab when the sidebar is closed. My two patches are deleted.\n- **Footer row.** The info panel's action icons now end on the image's bottom edge, which is the line you drew.\n- **The library behind can't be reached.** While an item is open, the library underneath ignores clicks and keyboard focus, so Tab can't land on hidden cards. It stays loaded so the item can still fly back into its card when you close it.\n- **Add still works over an item.** The Add window, the first-run welcome and the keyboard-shortcuts window had to move out of the library area, which is why `App.tsx` shows a big diff. The code itself is unchanged.\n- **Smoother opening.** At the start of each open, the image used to shrink inside the growing card for a moment before filling it. That was there before, and the new layout made it more visible. It now fills the card from the first frame.\n\n**Before and after, sidebar closed:**\n\n![Before](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\itemview\\before-closed.png)\n![After](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\itemview\\after-closed.png)\n\n**After, sidebar open, and mid-way through closing:**\n\n![After, sidebar open](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\itemview\\after-open.png)\n![Closing back into the card](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\itemview\\mid-close.png)\n\nI checked all of this in the desktop preview, including focus going back to the card after closing. The one thing I couldn't see is the note editing layout, because \"Edit note\" didn't open the editor with the preview's sample data. That layout uses the same new spacing, but it still needs a look in the full app.\n\nI also added a changelog line for this fix."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1082,"cache_read_input_tokens":170612,"output_tokens":842,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":26},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1082,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":842,"cache_read_input_tokens":170612,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1082,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1082},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgFxt13THWKadE1Kh17mN","requestRef":"b8954678-c437-428b-b7bd-53a3fdba7c40","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"20ab105e-7879-4291-a376-5456b0cfbbc9","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:51:07.396Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slu