{"parentUuid":"ea6ceb4e-1761-4a24-bcd4-03e3d22f3441","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01DLLfmYj28LQu2uCjxLsLAB","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"341a00c0-85a9-41c9-96b9-10e894985d9e","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:31:40.106Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"341a00c0-85a9-41c9-96b9-10e894985d9e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgG6XaTU7A9ur9nGVdjQU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm weighing two options for the Add menu flow: either the disclosure panel expands further to host the editor form once a type is chosen, or selecting a type simply opens the existing modal directly in that mode, though that risks a redundant picker inside the modal.\n\nThe cleanest approach: the disclosure panel keeps the mode grid, and selecting a type swaps the grid for the editor inline (with height animation and a back button), while File is special-cased to skip the editor entirely — clicking it triggers the OS file picker and persists immediately for instant capture, since saving should be faster than deciding. I'm also considering panel width (roughly 320px anchored near the Add button) and whether the quote editor's two inputs need to stack vertically to fit, and checking other callers of openCapture like the new-note keyboard shortcut to make sure this change doesn't break them.\n\nNow I'm working through the empty-state \"Add something\" buttons and how they call openCaptureModal, which assumes the sidebar disclosure is visible — but if the sidebar is closed, that disclosure doesn't exist on screen, so removing the compact capture-bar button breaks the closed-sidebar add flow. The fix is to have openCapture force the sidebar open (setIsSidebarOpen(true)) before showing the disclosure, which works fine even as a drawer on narrow layouts, and I'm also noting the disclosure should behave like a non-modal popover: closing on Escape or outside click, and returning focus to the Add button afterward.\n\nChecking the window keydown handler, I want to preserve isAdding as the gate for shortcuts and Escape handling, treating isAdding as equivalent to \"disclosure open,\" and keeping the capture error display and screenshot-disabled-while-capturing logic intact. For styling, I'm planning the panel to use our existing palette — outer surface color with a bordered header labeled \"Add to library\" plus a close button, and an inner grid area using a darker frame color — and animating the transition from the cream collapsed Add button into this darker expanded panel via a crossfade using shared layout IDs.\n\nNow I'm going through a list of bugs to fix: wiring up click handlers on the grid items since they currently do nothing, switching the list key from index to label, adding Escape/outside-click/focus management, and fixing the shared-layout animation so the label and content don't visually distort while scaling — I'll fade the inner content in after a short delay to hide the distortion. I also need to add proper ARIA attributes and button types, and review how defaultItems are handled.\n\nI'm also checking that defaultItems aren't being recreated on every render and dropping the autoPlay sync effect, confirming the collapsed button rendering inside AnimatePresence is fine, and keeping the layoutId border-radius styling since motion handles that correction automatically. I confirm motion/react and hugeicons are already available, and I still need to look up the MIT license copyright holder for Viora.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6007,"cache_read_input_tokens":196475,"output_tokens":2121,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1772},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6007,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2121,"cache_read_input_tokens":196475,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6007,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6007},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":23138,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgG6Xa8NgyiTke9gvXejV","requestRef":"34961bc8-3b9b-4e4e-bbb8-6c630a82ca29","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"667d2796-66b5-4344-bd08-8be294705478","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:31:40.105Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"667d2796-66b5-4344-bd08-8be294705478","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgG6XaTU7A9ur9nGVdjQU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've laid out the Add menu plan: the sidebar's Add button morphs into a panel with a grid of capture types, where Note/Link/Quote swap into inline forms while File and Screenshot trigger immediately. Now I'll check Viora's license text for the credit.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6007,"cache_read_input_tokens":196475,"output_tokens":2121,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1772},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6007,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2121,"cache_read_input_tokens":196475,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6007,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6007},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgG6Xa8NgyiTke9gvXejV","requestRef":"34961bc8-3b9b-4e4e-bbb8-6c630a82ca29","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b5778567-569f-4a12-84c2-b163f49d7f77","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:31:40.116Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
