{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"0adb2694630f10fc5c18f06b6a3fbc07e625be0d74a0c90656451240ec9db5ca","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm planning to extract a new AddMenu component since there are only a couple of callers for openCaptureModal plus the \"new-note\" shortcut and footer item to account for. Rather than passing many capture-related props down from App, I'm thinking AddMenu should manage its own draft state (title, url, quote fields) internally and call back into App only when needed.\n\nFor callbacks, I'm settling on something like onSaveNote, onSaveLink, onSaveQuote, onPickFile, and onScreenshot, each returning a promise so the menu can show a saving/error state itself. That should let me strip newTitle, newQuote fields, captureUrl, and selectedFile out of App's state entirely — I just need to grep for other places those are used, like paste handling, before removing them.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Next I'll check which of App's capture state only the modal uses, so the new menu can own it:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CsTfQDLiQaYYaAJQVmX77c","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && for v in newTitle setNewTitle newQuoteText setNewQuoteText newQuoteAttribution newQuoteSourceUrl captureUrl setCaptureUrl selectedFile setSelectedFile captureMode setCaptureMode isAdding setIsAdding captureNoteInputRef captureUrlInputRef captureQuoteInputRef fileInputRef captureError setCaptureError isCapturing showCaptureError CaptureMode; do echo \"$v: $(grep -n \"\\b$v\\b\" src/App.tsx | cut -d: -f1 | tr '\\n' ' ')\"; done"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
