{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","id":"4f27d4e6-db33-4869-b9f3-bb7dd9743614","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:32:05.698Z","version":"2.1.306","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"4325e2b9fcbda78c081d69a7cdc424779de8471fd78a037fce4545e52da59e6e","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"f9a9b49d-0ceb-4516-8293-b10ba3526c74","keep":335,"tail":["fa019a7fcaa13b9a0ae914324e8a869b0374679a1bd1d51f54d6b4e5e50950bf","b3bf4dfb947621e1ff794dea5eebd6b5caadb6641694c4bae89a1134edb25255","9df1a6e1b5e3082979de8fc19e117103c7f6cefb924d82fb7dc9b06a19ba0b9e"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",337,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"d51b2c537b2562138c343452e4ab8a214388df04947a1f29d66f5f94bcc18f54"}
{"parentUuid":"7f95bfa4-8121-4e84-a4ca-32a1fd53d83c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01VBTPQg1epB9EqQeJ6jYEJQ","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"df82fe0b-9e02-4abc-a091-4f565e368010","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:32:49.614Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"df82fe0b-9e02-4abc-a091-4f565e368010","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgG6bENrD8qSdwrerT9gS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm noting that saveCapture doesn't set isCapturing, and that the persist functions return promises rather than throwing synchronously. I'm sketching the AddMenu component's props interface, deciding to keep isAdding and captureMode in App state since the keyboard shortcut and Escape logic depend on them.\n\nI'm simplifying the design so AddMenu is controlled by App via open/mode/onOpenChange/onModeChange plus save handlers, with drafts kept internal. For Escape handling, I'll keep App's existing global handler but drop the focus-trap effect since this is non-modal now, while reconsidering the focus-return behavior — restoring focus to the Add button only makes sense when closing via Escape or the close button, not when closing via an outside click, so I'll let AddMenu manage its own focus restoration for those cases and do nothing on outside click.\n\nSo App's responsibility narrows to tracking isAdding/captureMode, providing openCapture(mode) that also opens the sidebar, and wiring up save handlers for notes, links, quotes, and file picks that call into the corresponding persist functions.\n\nI'm also planning the cleanup: screenshot capture stays as a simple trigger, errors are surfaced via an `error` prop on AddMenu while the actual saveCapture logic and persist functions remain in App. I need to strip out now-unused state and refs from App — draft fields like newTitle/newQuote*/captureUrl/selectedFile, the various capture refs, and the modal focus-trap effects — while making sure AddMenu stays mounted at all times (even collapsed) so its internal draft state survives closing. Finally I'm figuring out where AddMenu actually renders in place of the old add-button inside the sidebar footer, given the sidebar's visibility toggling.\n\nFor positioning, I'm keeping the collapsed button in normal flow while the expanded panel goes absolute within a relative wrapper that preserves the button's footprint, so `layoutId` morphing between the two works smoothly with motion's layout projection. Then I'm reasoning through the stacking context: since the sidebar is absolutely positioned with z-index auto and the main frame paints after it in DOM order, the panel needs an explicit z-index to guarantee it layers above the main frame rather than relying on paint order.\n\nNow I'm debating panel width — letting it overlap the frame edge by roughly 80px gives it a popover feel similar to Viora's demo, versus constraining it to the sidebar's 212px width with a tighter 3-column grid of smaller tiles (~65px each) if I want it to stay contained.\n\nI'm leaning toward keeping the panel inside the sidebar width since it avoids z-index headaches and feels more integrated, even if it's smaller than Viora's bigger card style. With five items in a 3-column grid, the last row ends up with two tiles left-aligned (Note, Link, Quote / File, Screenshot), and the overall panel height works out to roughly 200px with the header and two grid rows.\n\nFor the editor view, I'm picturing a header with a back chevron, a contextual title like \"New note\" or \"Save a link\", and a close X, with the body holding inputs and a Save button that animates height as the layout changes. For the morph animation between the collapsed button and the open panel, I'm thinking of using a shared layoutId so both states crossfade smoothly despite the color change from cream to dark.\n\nTo avoid distorting the panel content during the layout animation, I'll delay the content's opacity fade-in slightly (around 0.08s) so any early distortion is masked, and keep the spring transition consistent with the rest of the app's motion character (bounce 0.1, duration 0.4) rather than switching to a plain ease curve.\n\nFor the label morph, I'm debating whether \"Add\" should transform into the header title via layoutId -- keeping the same short text avoids distortion from width mismatches, so I'll keep the header label simply as \"Add\" across both collapsed and editor states, possibly with a back button preceding it in editor mode.\n\nIn editor mode the header label switches to the mode name with a back chevron, and closing crossfades it back to \"Add\" rather than doing a layout morph. For reduced motion, I'm relying on MotionConfig's reducedMotion=\"user\" setting at the root to disable layout/transform animations automatically. For accessibility, I'm setting aria-expanded and aria-controls on the collapsed button, moving focus into the first tile on open, and restoring focus back to the button on close via a ref and effect tied to the open state.\n\nNow I'm working through the panel's dialog semantics, the Escape key handling tied to the app's capture-mode state, and the tricky focus-return logic needed since the panel exits via AnimatePresence while still mounted — checking whether focus was inside the panel before it unmounts, then redirecting it to the trigger once that remounts in the same commit.\n\nI also need outside-click dismissal without focus restoration, a disabled \"Saving…\" state while capturing, and the hidden file input wired up so picking a file calls onPickFile and closes the menu.\n\nScreenshot tile triggers the capture flow and closes the menu too. For global handlers, Escape should back out of a mode first before closing entirely, and shortcuts stay blocked while isAdding is true; capture errors show inline within the menu instead of the capture bar, and the input should autofocus when switching into a mode.\n\nSince autoFocus triggers accessibility lint warnings, I should use a ref with a layout effect instead. Opening a capture mode should also open the sidebar, which already handles mobile drawer behavior fine. I need to strip out the now-unused compact add button styles, and clean up the leftover whitespace in list view afterward.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":953,"cache_read_input_tokens":210239,"output_tokens":3859,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3742},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":953,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3859,"cache_read_input_tokens":210239,"cache_creation_input_tokens":953,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":953},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":43104,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgG6bDbiZZ787d7WLVQSu","requestRef":"4f27d4e6-db33-4869-b9f3-bb7dd9743614","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"29be0c69-1099-4a15-b5fb-eb0dfb2071d0","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:32:49.613Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"29be0c69-1099-4a15-b5fb-eb0dfb2071d0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgG6bENrD8qSdwrerT9gS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Since the modal's drafts and focus logic are only used by the modal itself, I'll move that state into the new menu and have it call App's save functions directly. Next, I'll check the Add button and sidebar footer styles.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":953,"cache_read_input_tokens":210239,"output_tokens":3859,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3742},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":953,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3859,"cache_read_input_tokens":210239,"cache_creation_input_tokens":953,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":953},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgG6bDbiZZ787d7WLVQSu","requestRef":"4f27d4e6-db33-4869-b9f3-bb7dd9743614","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5edcb937-43de-4b19-bc52-1581d22ed863","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:32:49.624Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
