{"parentUuid":"20314e59-f756-4fe7-8a54-c51572c6c53c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d217de97-c69e-4ffb-8cab-90ef6199535a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LHzQd2RmPnuEUTDigyyXup","type":"tool_result","content":"206-  return true;\n207-};\n208-const clickCaptureOption = (title) => {\n209:  const option = [...document.querySelectorAll(\".capture-option\")].find(\n210-    (node) => node.querySelector(\"strong\")?.textContent === title,\n211-  );\n212-  if (!option) return false;\n213-  option.click();\n214-  return true;\n215-};\n216-const setInputValue = (selector, value) => {\n217-  const el = document.querySelector(selector);\n218-  if (!el) return false;\n219-  const setter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(HTMLInputElement.prototype, \"value\").set;\n220-  setter.call(el, value);\n221-  el.dispatchEvent(new Event(\"input\", { bubbles: true }));\n--\n353-    const noteText = \"ui smoke note\";\n354-    await step(\"note is created and appears in the grid\", async () => {\n355-      await cdp.evaluate(clickSelector, 'button[title=\"Add something to your library\"]');\n356:      await waitFor(\"add menu\", hasSelector, \".capture-option\");\n357-      await cdp.evaluate(clickCaptureOption, \"Note\");\n358-      await waitFor(\"note input\", hasSelector, 'input[aria-label=\"New note\"]');\n359-      await cdp.evaluate(setInputValue, 'input[aria-label=\"New note\"]', noteText);\n360-      await cdp.send(\"Input.dispatchKeyEvent\", {\n361-        type: \"keyDown\",\n362-        key: \"Enter\",\n363-        code: \"Enter\",\n364-        windowsVirtualKeyCode: 13,\n365-        text: \"\\r\",\n366-      });\n367-      await cdp.send(\"Input.dispatchKeyEvent\", {\n368-        type: \"keyUp\",\n=====\n# Capture a note from the Add menu\r\n\r\n## Sub-features\r\n\r\n- Note tile in the Add to your library dialog.\r\n- Save to library button; the card appears before any processing finishes.\r\n\r\n## How to get to it (user POV)\r\n\r\nClick Add in the top bar. The dialog offers Note, Link, File, Quote, and Screenshot. Choose Note, type a line, and press Save to library. The new card lands at the top of Everything.\r\n\r\n## Driving it with `scripts/drive.mjs`\r\n\r\nSave as `steps.json`, then run with a fresh evidence dir:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n[\r\n  {\"label\": \"open Add\", \"click\": \"button[title='Add something to your library']\"},\r\n  {\"label\": \"choose Note\", \"clickText\": {\"selector\": \"button\", \"text\": \"Write something to remember\"}},\r\n  {\"label\": \"note field\", \"wait\": \"input[aria-label='New note']\"},\r\n  {\"label\": \"type note\", \"fill\": \"input[aria-label='New note']\", \"text\": \"verify-inkling probe note\"},\r\n  {\"label\": \"save\", \"click\": \"button.capture-save[type='submit']\"},\r\n  {\"label\": \"card shows\", \"expect\": \"[...document.querySelectorAll('article')].some(a => a.textContent.includes('verify-inkling probe note'))\", \"timeoutMs\": 10000},\r\n  {\"label\": \"shot\", \"shot\": \"note-saved.png\"}\r\n]\r\n```\r\n\r\nEnd state proof: the card with the text is in the grid, and `items` has one row with `kind = 'note'`, `body = 'verify-inkling probe note'`, `body_format = 'md'`, `archived = 0`. The title stays null for notes.\r\n\r\n## Gotchas\r\n\r\n- Note title is null; the text lives in `body`. Check `body`, not `title`.\r\n- The dialog only appears on Add. The Add button has a title, not visible text.\r\n- Link, File, Quote, and Screenshot are not driven by this map yet.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"73fa12bd-d13b-40f3-8557-70f5da933269","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:33:04.957Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"206-  return true;\n207-};\n208-const clickCaptureOption = (title) => {\n209:  const option = [...document.querySelectorAll(\".capture-option\")].find(\n210-    (node) => node.querySelector(\"strong\")?.textContent === title,\n211-  );\n212-  if (!option) return false;\n213-  option.click();\n214-  return true;\n215-};\n216-const setInputValue = (selector, value) => {\n217-  const el = document.querySelector(selector);\n218-  if (!el) return false;\n219-  const setter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(HTMLInputElement.prototype, \"value\").set;\n220-  setter.call(el, value);\n221-  el.dispatchEvent(new Event(\"input\", { bubbles: true }));\n--\n353-    const noteText = \"ui smoke note\";\n354-    await step(\"note is created and appears in the grid\", async () => {\n355-      await cdp.evaluate(clickSelector, 'button[title=\"Add something to your library\"]');\n356:      await waitFor(\"add menu\", hasSelector, \".capture-option\");\n357-      await cdp.evaluate(clickCaptureOption, \"Note\");\n358-      await waitFor(\"note input\", hasSelector, 'input[aria-label=\"New note\"]');\n359-      await cdp.evaluate(setInputValue, 'input[aria-label=\"New note\"]', noteText);\n360-      await cdp.send(\"Input.dispatchKeyEvent\", {\n361-        type: \"keyDown\",\n362-        key: \"Enter\",\n363-        code: \"Enter\",\n364-        windowsVirtualKeyCode: 13,\n365-        text: \"\\r\",\n366-      });\n367-      await cdp.send(\"Input.dispatchKeyEvent\", {\n368-        type: \"keyUp\",\n=====\n# Capture a note from the Add menu\r\n\r\n## Sub-features\r\n\r\n- Note tile in the Add to your library dialog.\r\n- Save to library button; the card appears before any processing finishes.\r\n\r\n## How to get to it (user POV)\r\n\r\nClick Add in the top bar. The dialog offers Note, Link, File, Quote, and Screenshot. Choose Note, type a line, and press Save to library. The new card lands at the top of Everything.\r\n\r\n## Driving it with `scripts/drive.mjs`\r\n\r\nSave as `steps.json`, then run with a fresh evidence dir:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n[\r\n  {\"label\": \"open Add\", \"click\": \"button[title='Add something to your library']\"},\r\n  {\"label\": \"choose Note\", \"clickText\": {\"selector\": \"button\", \"text\": \"Write something to remember\"}},\r\n  {\"label\": \"note field\", \"wait\": \"input[aria-label='New note']\"},\r\n  {\"label\": \"type note\", \"fill\": \"input[aria-label='New note']\", \"text\": \"verify-inkling probe note\"},\r\n  {\"label\": \"save\", \"click\": \"button.capture-save[type='submit']\"},\r\n  {\"label\": \"card shows\", \"expect\": \"[...document.querySelectorAll('article')].some(a => a.textContent.includes('verify-inkling probe note'))\", \"timeoutMs\": 10000},\r\n  {\"label\": \"shot\", \"shot\": \"note-saved.png\"}\r\n]\r\n```\r\n\r\nEnd state proof: the card with the text is in the grid, and `items` has one row with `kind = 'note'`, `body = 'verify-inkling probe note'`, `body_format = 'md'`, `archived = 0`. The title stays null for notes.\r\n\r\n## Gotchas\r\n\r\n- Note title is null; the text lives in `body`. Check `body`, not `title`.\r\n- The dialog only appears on Add. The Add button has a title, not visible text.\r\n- Link, File, Quote, and Screenshot are not driven by this map yet.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"20314e59-f756-4fe7-8a54-c51572c6c53c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
