{"parentUuid":"385bf1b1-0479-43de-b8f5-1a741e4c10ed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgG6iPkM28GXRY5QXMwYe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I notice saveCapture doesn't set isCapturing since it calls persistArticle rather than captureFile/captureArticle, so I need to write handlers that return success booleans and set captureError appropriately. I also want to check how the global Escape handler interacts with the reading item and selection state.\n\nFor focus management, I plan to add a useLayoutEffect in AddMenu that focuses the first tile whenever the panel opens without a mode and the panel doesn't already contain focus, which naturally covers both the initial opening case and returning from a form. Now I'm reworking the App-level state: consolidating CaptureMode into the AddMode type since file is no longer a separate mode, and removing the old drafts, refs, and focus effects that are now redundant.\n\nI'm also stripping out the old capture modal logic entirely — captureModalRef, fileInputRef, saveCapture, selectCaptureMode, and related handlers — while adjusting openCapture to open the sidebar instead and dropping setSelectedFile/setCaptureUrl from the respective capture functions. I'm adding a saveFromAddMenu helper that wraps the save call, clears errors, and resets adding state on success or surfaces the error message on failure, then rendering the new AddMenu component in place of the old add button and modal JSX, cleaning up now-unused icon imports along the way. I'll need to go through the file section by section to make these edits carefully.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4733,"cache_read_input_tokens":223255,"output_tokens":1414,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":902},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0}