{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"ad87c8c15a072219877766f3686ef30086676a5dd02c91d18fcd6522dbd7c64e","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to move the margin-bottom from the add-button to the add-menu wrapper, and I'm noticing a potential conflict: Framer Motion sets inline transform styles during layout animation, which could override the CSS :active scale effect on the button. I should use the dedicated `scale` property instead to avoid that clash.\n\nNow I'm working through the AddMenu.css structure—positioning the panel absolutely within the wrapper, sizing the button to fill its container, and styling the dropdown panel with surface colors, border, padding, and shadow to match the design reference, while checking what the actual theme variable values are for the surface and frame colors.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Next, the menu's styles. Checking the palette variables to match the sidebar:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01K6qseWfprNbTbWbCwyZ1fP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && sed -n 6,80p src/App.css | grep -n \"library-\\|--ink\\|--green\\|--orange\\|--sidebar-radius\\|--glass-active\\|--muted\\|--font\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
