{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"7c8280b8d514ca4eefed2540f73868336fc5597daf9fe907fd461f71baf3ba1a","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see the issue: the image's intrinsic height is leaking into the grid row because it's in-flow with percent height. The fix is to absolutely position the image to fill its wrapper in list mode so the wrap relies on min-height instead, and I need to apply the same treatment to video elements and check the card content's min-height too.\n\nGiven the whitespace complaint, I should make the list row more compact — smaller min-height, tighter padding, and a flex column layout for the content with the footer pushed to the bottom using margin-top:auto so spacing stays consistent regardless of description length.\n\nI'll pin the footer with flex instead of margin and measure the resulting row height to confirm it tightens up properly.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found the bug: the list view image is positioned absolutely, so it doesn't drive the row's height, causing the footer to stay pinned when a long note expands the row. I'll fix the image's positioning so the row sizes properly.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014jq9MjvUfffxS5A1RpxUf2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && grep -n \"card-image\\b\\|className=\\\"card-image\\\"\\|card-image \" src/components/ItemMedia.tsx | head; python - <<'EOF'\nimport io\np='src/App.css'\ns=io.open(p,encoding='utf-8',newline='').read()\na='''.list-mode .card-content {\n  display: block;\n  min-height: 155px;\n}'''\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,'''/* The image covers its cell instead of sizing the row, so a tall photo cannot\n   stretch the row; the text sets the height and the footer keeps to the bottom. */\n.list-mode .card-image-wrap > .card-image {\n  position: absolute;\n  inset: 0;\n}\n.list-mode .card-content {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  min-height: 0;\n}\n.list-mode .card-content .card-footer {\n  margin-top: auto;\n}\n.list-mode .card-content > :nth-last-child(2) {\n  margin-bottom: 14px;\n}''')\nio.open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8',newline='').write(s)\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
