{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"cd4f832d9481d52455d98994cb94e80ed8df005c93266fa82223dcfd4b7378be","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The nth-last-child approach feels fragile, so I'm considering alternatives like making the footer's margin-top adaptive or having the preceding element grow to fill space instead.\n\nI think I've found a cleaner trick: use a flex pseudo-element spacer with order properties so it sits between the content and footer, guaranteeing a minimum gap regardless of whether row height is driven by content or media size.\n\nFor the image height, I'm deciding to separate the rules for `card-image-wrap` from `card-paper-art` -- paper-art variants need their own min-height since they have richer internal content, but plain image wraps can drop to a lower floor like 120px so rows with little text don't carry excess whitespace.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The `:nth-last-child` margin is fragile. I'll replace it with a flex spacer, and give image cells a lower floor so a photo with little text still gets a reasonable thumbnail:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MZUmJz7MuwQoZbac9TttqH","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && python - <<'EOF'\nimport io\np='src/App.css'\ns=io.open(p,encoding='utf-8',newline='').read()\na='''.list-mode .card-content .card-footer {\n  margin-top: auto;\n}\n.list-mode .card-content > :nth-last-child(2) {\n  margin-bottom: 14px;\n}'''\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,'''/* A spacer ahead of the footer: at least 14px, and all the slack when the\n   artwork makes the row taller. */\n.list-mode .card-content::after {\n  content: \"\";\n  flex: 1 0 14px;\n  order: 1;\n}\n.list-mode .card-content .card-footer {\n  order: 2;\n  margin-top: 0;\n}''')\na='''.list-mode .card-image-wrap > .card-image {'''\ns=s.replace(a,'''.list-mode .card-image-wrap {\n  min-height: 120px;\n}\n'''+a,1)\nio.open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8',newline='').write(s)\nEOF\nsed -n '/List view: 155px/,/featured-card .card-content {/p' src/App.css | head -60"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
