{"parentUuid":"a6019bf4-9997-4d1c-9afc-b4d6162484d0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d217de97-c69e-4ffb-8cab-90ef6199535a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VUVg47BJj4NZcCn8TaR47w","type":"tool_result","content":"The operation completed successfully.\r\r\ncleaned\nChecked 6 files in 123ms. No fixes applied.\n16:- Keep an `Unreleased` section at the top; move entries under a version heading at release time\n17-\n18-Guardrails:\n19-- Never mention that changes were made by an AI agent or even a developer — write entries as if the changes were just made\n20-- Don't editorialize or pad entries to look more substantial than the change was\n21-- If a change is trivial (typo fix, formatting, comment-only), skip the changelog — not every commit needs an entry\n22-- Ask before rewriting or reordering existing changelog history when you notice it is drifting from the required structure; only append.\n23-- When restructuring this document NO important/crucial/technical details should be lost\n24-\n25-\n26-\n27:## Unreleased\n28-\n29-### Added\n30-\n31-- Right-click a card to read, favorite, open its link, copy its link, show it in its folder, or archive it (#170)\n32-- Buttons show a short label on hover or keyboard focus, in the same glass as the controls around them (#170)\n33-- Settings → General → Open source licenses lists every shipped dependency, vendored component, and bundled model with its license text and source, searchable and filterable by license (#170)\n34-- Settings → Appearance switches components between alternative looks while we compare them, starting with the grid/list toggle as the current pill or a coss ui segmented control (#170)\n35-- First-run welcome flow on first launch of the installed app, replayable from Settings → General\n36-- PDF cards now show page-one thumbnails generated in the background after capture; existing PDFs are backfilled one at a time when the job queue is idle.\n37-- Chrome MV3 extension saves a page or right-clicked link through inkling's local capture receiver, with the existing capture link as fallback.\n38-- `bun run ui:smoke` drives the core library flows in Electron against a scratch profile and fails on console errors\n39-- Electron desktop shell alongside Tauri, with scoped `app://` assets, an IPC command allowlist, and `inkling://` capture links.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3acae082-cac3-4767-96e6-8ef546e85c3a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:42:13.263Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"The operation completed successfully.\r\r\ncleaned\nChecked 6 files in 123ms. No fixes applied.\n16:- Keep an `Unreleased` section at the top; move entries under a version heading at release time\n17-\n18-Guardrails:\n19-- Never mention that changes were made by an AI agent or even a developer — write entries as if the changes were just made\n20-- Don't editorialize or pad entries to look more substantial than the change was\n21-- If a change is trivial (typo fix, formatting, comment-only), skip the changelog — not every commit needs an entry\n22-- Ask before rewriting or reordering existing changelog history when you notice it is drifting from the required structure; only append.\n23-- When restructuring this document NO important/crucial/technical details should be lost\n24-\n25-\n26-\n27:## Unreleased\n28-\n29-### Added\n30-\n31-- Right-click a card to read, favorite, open its link, copy its link, show it in its folder, or archive it (#170)\n32-- Buttons show a short label on hover or keyboard focus, in the same glass as the controls around them (#170)\n33-- Settings → General → Open source licenses lists every shipped dependency, vendored component, and bundled model with its license text and source, searchable and filterable by license (#170)\n34-- Settings → Appearance switches components between alternative looks while we compare them, starting with the grid/list toggle as the current pill or a coss ui segmented control (#170)\n35-- First-run welcome flow on first launch of the installed app, replayable from Settings → General\n36-- PDF cards now show page-one thumbnails generated in the background after capture; existing PDFs are backfilled one at a time when the job queue is idle.\n37-- Chrome MV3 extension saves a page or right-clicked link through inkling's local capture receiver, with the existing capture link as fallback.\n38-- `bun run ui:smoke` drives the core library flows in Electron against a scratch profile and fails on console errors\n39-- Electron desktop shell alongside Tauri, with scoped `app://` assets, an IPC command allowlist, and `inkling://` capture links.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a6019bf4-9997-4d1c-9afc-b4d6162484d0","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
