{"parentUuid":"1d548d15-128d-4a3f-bc3f-0c8f3fe29a5c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgG9Br3t5K1RZPQpaVL6x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The drag region spans the top 32px, so if the stage extends there it's fine since it's just background with the image padded away from that edge, and zoom controls sit at the bottom anyway. I should check whether the titlebar height variable actually applies outside Electron, since in browser preview it might be zero.\n\nNow I'm working out how the stage frame's radius should relate to its inset gap — with an 8px gap, the frame's 16px corner radius minus the gap gives a tight 7-8px stage radius, which feels small compared to the current 20px. I'm leaning toward a gap of 8px with a slightly larger stage radius like 12, accepting it won't be perfectly concentric but will still look clean.\n\nI also need to adjust stage padding so the enlarged image area doesn't crowd the zoom control at the bottom, keep the inspector's top clearing the window controls while aligning its bottom to the stage, and account for the sidebar-open state shifting the left inset. I'll add new inset variables for the stage and inspector tops, make sure editing-note mode inherits them properly, and remove the old 43px media query rule.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":774,"cache_read_input_tokens":86287,"output_tokens":2077,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":860},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":774,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2077,"cache_read_input_tokens":86287,"cache_creation_input_tokens":774,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_t