{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","prNumber":170,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Squidys-Tools/inkling/pull/170","prRepository":"Squidys-Tools/inkling","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:12:12.185Z"}
{"parentUuid":"7aaf2796-49a8-444e-b6e6-c916157d28ee","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgG9eaLLDs3C2Z1hV38EV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The sidebar tab no longer shows over an open item, and the photo area now uses that empty space. I committed and pushed both to #170 (`becb68d`, plus a one-line comment cleanup in `5520c2f`).\n\n- **Sidebar button:** while an item is open with the sidebar closed, the button isn't shown at all. Closing the item brings it back.\n- **Photo area:** it now sits 8px from the frame on the top, left and bottom, with the sidebar open or closed. Before, it started 35px down to stay below the window controls, and 43px in when the sidebar was closed. The details panel on the right is the only part that still starts below the window controls. The minimize, maximize and close buttons sit above it, so they never cover the photo.\n- **The photo itself:** it gets 60px of room above and below instead of 72px, so it's a bit bigger. The zoom control still sits clear of it.\n\n![Item view, sidebar closed](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\itemview\\closed.png)\n![Item view, sidebar open](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\itemview\\fort.png)\n\nOne thing to know: with the sidebar closed and an item open, there's now no on-screen way to open the sidebar. It comes back when you close the item, or when you press N.\n\nI checked this in the desktop app against a scratch library: opening an item, closing the sidebar while it's open, and closing the item. Typecheck and Biome pass, and I updated the existing changelog line.\n\nDuring cleanup the scratch app took over the `inkling://` link handler in the registry, and the usual restore step failed. I put the handler back from an earlier backup, and it again points at this worktree's Electron, as it did before."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":635,"cache_read_input_tokens":119880,"output_tokens":579,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":635,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":579,"cache_read_input_tokens":119880,"cache_creation_input_tokens":635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":635},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgG9ea3i5MaZvExhADd36","requestRef":"ba250112-5653-4c36-b373-99d23616f235","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"abd49a50-0d36-4b0e-8a67-f4ea42f3dbb8","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:12:17.944Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
