{"parentUuid":"8afe4bf7-ed4f-4b4a-aad5-c8958e64dbd3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGBfK8YLg5fpoB9P2j3c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to check whether LiquidGlass tracks DOM changes with a MutationObserver so dynamically added elements like tooltips get picked up—since tooltips appear on demand, it likely needs to rescan. For the context menu, since it's portaled to the body and rendered above the library stage, I should make it a `.glass` element rendered into a container tied to the target roots.\n\nThe simplest fix is to have App wrap a layer div for the context menu similar to the tooltip layer, and either pass that container into createPortal or drop the portal entirely since only one usage exists. I'll settle on removing the dedicated portal target prop and rendering the menu within App's own layer div, since its fixed positioning means DOM placement doesn't affect layout.\n\nI also need to check how `.glass` vs `.css-glass` behave — when liquid glass rendering is active, `.glass` elements lose their CSS backdrop since the native effect handles it, but `.css-glass` stays as a plain fallback outside the stage. Since the context menu could open near the library stage edges and potentially overlap the sidebar when flipped, I need to make sure its glass class matches the backdrop it's actually sitting over.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2721,"cache_read_input_tokens":147042,"output_tokens":1261,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1039},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2721,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1261,"cache_read_input_tokens":147042,"cache_creation_i