{"parentUuid":"db757815-f816-4b68-a694-ede1c3796559","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGBhBGKkNAaTcKzjiscL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"That legacy positioning for sidebar-toggle looks off, so I'm redesigning it as a glass circle sitting inside the capture bar, centered vertically with absolute positioning, consistent across desktop and mobile. I need to strip out the old mobile overrides that were shifting its left offset.\n\nI'm also removing the rule hiding sidebar-close and sidebar-toggle, giving sidebar-close consistent base sizing, and making it hover-only on desktop by fading opacity until the sidebar is hovered or focused, while keeping it fully visible on mobile. The brand lockup and close button placement look fine at the current sidebar width, so now I'm writing the sidebar-toggle styles as an absolutely positioned glass circle anchored to the capture bar's left edge with hover and active states.\n\nI need to strip out the leftover mobile-specific left offsets for sidebar-toggle in a couple places, confirm the toggle sits above the capture bar without needing extra z-index since pointer-events are already enabled on its children, and add tooltip labels for opening and closing the sidebar. Then I'm planning to fully remove the old edge-tab component, its CSS block, and the conditional rendering for it in the main App file.\n\nAlso need to update the changelog entry describing the closed sidebar's tab stepping out of the way, and check for lingering edge-tab references in the smoke tests, skills, and other test files.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1586,"cache_read_input_tokens":153880,"output_tokens":1177,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":955},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard