{"parentUuid":"ac080a0f-b3f7-4880-b5a5-70004d7286f1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGBwhjmztUSCF5qNww2k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This could explain it—if the window is hidden at launch, requestAnimationFrame won't fire so the retry loop stalls, and Virtuoso's ResizeObserver may not trigger either, leaving the grid unscrollable when apply() runs. That likely mirrors the user's real app, where the window shows only after the page has already rendered while hidden, so I need to make the fix robust to that scenario.\n\nInstead of a raf loop, I should hold scroll position via ResizeObserver until the layout stabilizes, releasing on actual user input, since RO callbacks tied to rendering steps naturally pause while hidden and resume once shown. I'll watch the grid's growing children for size changes, and release the hold on wheel, pointerdown, or keydown events so user scrolling always takes priority over the correction.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1601,"cache_read_input_tokens":171870,"output_tokens":1794,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":558},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1601,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1794,"cache_read_input_tokens":171870,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1601,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1601},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":8967,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGBwhGFnLwqGc3GekwtB","requestRef":"1e7e9cdd-bef2-465b-9e73-91f2d8201646",