{"parentUuid":"ebc66704-49a0-4669-a32f-5585fbc0ab37","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGBzv2ntXN1yDRCjXjGY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm wondering if the ResizeObserver simply never fires because the element stays hidden the whole time — visibility never changes to trigger it, which would explain why the hold value stays stuck at 0 even after the delay, whereas a genuinely visible window would let RO fire normally.\n\nThe hidden state itself is suspicious though — maybe the scratch Electron window is occluded behind T3, and bringToFront via CDP doesn't actually raise a native window, so visibility never flips. Rather than rely on RO alone, I could also listen for visibilitychange to trigger the hold, but that still might not be necessary since RO should fire once rendering actually happens. To actually verify this, I want to try forcing the window visible using the CDP Browser domain — maybe getWindowForTarget plus setWindowBounds with windowState \"normal\" will un-minimize it.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":822,"cache_read_input_tokens":176103,"output_tokens":825,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":598},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":822,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":825,"cache_read_input_tokens":176103,"cache_creation_input_tokens":822,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":822},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":9850,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGBzujvJLmXZRsx5PMs