t row\\|Right-click\" docs/changelog.md | head","description":"Clean up scratch, restore registry, scan changelog"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgGCSdxd2yEqWL141oSJ7","requestRef":"5a4a607c-7b3e-4f54-9127-65d82d0f3745","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"t3-code","attributionMcpTool":"html_render","type":"assistant","uuid":"30d548dc-7c6c-47f3-ba18-72d1cede1ee2","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:48:57.459Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"30d548dc-7c6c-47f3-ba18-72d1cede1ee2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a271f561-7394-4a86-b340-1226577b65b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VuU4gW9JEZHrcpmoYouRu9","type":"tool_result","content":"The operation completed successfully.\r\r\n3:All notable development phases and changes are recorded here. See also [roadmap.md](roadmap.md) for what comes next.\n9:4. When a change alters public behavior: API contracts, CLI flags, config options, env vars; anything a user of the project depends on being stable\n31:- Right-click a card to read, favorite, open its link, copy its link, show it in its folder, or archive it (#170)\n46:- Library export from Settings (Data tab): writes a dated folder with a consistent SQLite snapshot, the asset files the saved items reference, and a manifest of counts and sizes, after picking a destination folder in a native dialog.\n47:- Library restore from Settings (Data tab) imports items, assets, and Spaces without replacing existing items, verifies hashes in new exports, and flags assets in older exports that cannot be verified (SQU-119).\n49:- Portable Windows PR previews build a self-contained review folder with pinned ONNX Runtime and embedding models, isolated database/assets/models, and a `preview:win` artifact link.\n63:- Committed web-preview demo library: 24 personal items (photos, art, UI references, one clip) plus four keepers from the original set, shuffled with a fixed seed so the order is mixed but stable; images live compressed by hand in `public/seed-demo/` with titles in `src/seedPersonal.ts` (`src/seedPersonal.ts`, `src/App.tsx`, `public/seed-demo/`)\n77:- An open item takes over the whole library frame instead of floating inside it, so the sidebar tab, grid/list toggle and the selected card no longer show around its edges, and its stage fills the frame with an even margin while the closed sidebar's tab steps out of the way (#170)\n116:- Library opens faster on large libraries: the full-text index is built once on first run instead of being wiped and rebuilt every launch, and background job restarts no longer pay a reindex on their 5-second wake cycle (measured ~655 ms to ~16 ms to reopen a 1,000-item database) (`src-tauri/src/storage.rs`)\n120:- Library grid and list views soften into a progressive blur at the top edge, under the search bar, and the bottom edge, down to the window's last pixel; both stay in place while scrolling (`src/components/LibraryEdgeFade.tsx`, `src/components/GradualBlur/`, `src/App.css`, `src/App.tsx`)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a25fb252-8b88-4767-bac1-b07b523df468","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:49:00.444Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"The operation completed successfully.\r\r\n3:All notable development phases and changes are recorded here. See also [roadmap.md](roadmap.md) for what comes next.\n9:4. When a change alters public behavior: API contracts, CLI flags, config options, env vars; anything a user of the project depends on being stable\n31:- Right-click a card to read, favorite, open its link, copy its link, show it in its folder, or archive it (#170)\n46:- Library export from Settings (Data tab): writes a dated folder with a consistent SQLite snapshot, the asset files the saved items reference, and a manifest of counts and sizes, after picking a destination folder in a native dialog.\n47:- Library restore from Settings (Data tab) imports items, assets, and Spaces without replacing existing items, verifies hashes in new exports, and flags assets in older exports that cannot be verified (SQU-119).\n49:- Portable Windows PR previews build a self-contained review folder with pinned ONNX Runtime and embedding models, isolated database/assets/models, and a `preview:win` artifact link.\n63:- Committed web-preview demo library: 24 personal items (photos, art, UI references, one clip) plus four keepers from the original set, shuffled with a fixed seed so the order is mixed but stable; images live compressed by hand in `public/seed-demo/` with titles in `src/seedPersonal.ts` (`src/seedPersonal.ts`, `src/App.tsx`, `public/seed-demo/`)\n77:- An open item takes over the whole library frame instead of floating inside it, so the sidebar tab, grid/list toggle and the selected card no longer show around its edges, and its stage fills the frame with an even margin while the closed sidebar's tab steps out of the way (#170)\n116:- Library opens faster on large libraries: the full-text index is built once on first run instead of being wiped and rebuilt every launch, and background job restarts no longer pay a reindex on their 5-second wake cycle (measured ~655 ms to ~16 ms to reopen a 1,000-item database) (`src-tauri/src/storage.rs`)\n120:- Library grid and list views soften into a progressive blur at the top edge, under the search bar, and the bottom edge, down to the window's last pixel; both stay in place while scrolling (`src/components/LibraryEdgeFade.tsx`, `src/components/GradualBlur/`, `src/App.css`, `src/App.tsx`)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"30d548dc-7c6c-47f3-ba18-72d1cede1ee2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
