{"parentUuid":"c56d1360-8e8a-404e-a65e-388e18334bf4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"90b0958d-c8b0-412b-a194-a933a6711bc6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, Bash, Edit, Grep, PowerShell, Read, SendMessage, TaskStop, ToolSearch, WebFetch, WebSearch, Write, mcp__col__get_component, mcp__col__get_library, mcp__col__search_components, mcp__col__search_libraries, mcp__paper__find_nodes, mcp__paper__get_guide, mcp__paper__get_screenshot, mcp__paper__get_tree_summary, mcp__paper__open_file, mcp__t3-code__delegate_task, mcp__t3-code__html_preview, mcp__t3-code__html_render, mcp__t3-code__link_pull_request, mcp__t3-code__orchestrator_capabilities, mcp__t3-code__preview_click, mcp__t3-code__preview_evaluate, mcp__t3-code__preview_open, mcp__t3-code__preview_resize, mcp__t3-code__preview_snapshot, mcp__t3-code__preview_status, mcp__t3-code__task_status</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Branch and push rules:** work on branch `feat/glass-surface`, PR #170. Standing instruction: \"commit and push to 170 when your done just not to 174 yet\".\n   - **Done this session, in order:**\n     - **Item view (`becb68d`, `5520c2f`):**\n       - Hide the sidebar close button when the sidebar is closed and an item is open.\n       - The item stage uses the whitespace: an even 8px inset, and only the inspector drops below the window-controls band.\n     - **Mockup:** showed sidebar toggle styling options A–E.\n     - **Option C and related fixes (`4c6669a`):**\n       - Header close button beside the wordmark, visible on sidebar hover or focus.\n       - Liquid-glass open button at the toolbar's left.\n       - Edge tab removed.\n       - Focus hands off between the two buttons.\n       - \"put the library by default at this height\", the titlebar line at y≈37.\n       - Sidebar button in liquid glass.\n       - Right-click menu in liquid glass.\n       - Hi-fi mockup of D, rendered as HTML.\n     - **Settings → Appearance \"Sidebar button\": Buttons (C) / Edge grip (D) (`1f58397`):**\n       - Added so the user can compare them later.\n       - Also added the Ctrl+\\ (⌘+\\) sidebar shortcut.\n     - **\"the library can still scroll down more, i dont want that\" (`56a2639`):** removed the 52px rest gap and the scroll-hold effect, so the first row rests at the top and can't be pulled down.\n   - **CURRENT request (latest user message, with screenshot of edge grip mode, sidebar open, hovered):** \"when the sidebar is opened that should ever so slightly be over to the right, in the library side\". A hand-drawn mark is slightly right of the grip bar. The open-state edge grip (bar, and probably knob) should sit slightly further right, inside the library frame instead of straddling the border.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Stack:** Electron preview, React 19, motion/react, plain CSS, hugeicons.\n   - **Liquid glass (`LiquidGlass.tsx`):** draws under `.glass` elements in `targetRoots`; it moves the content into a `<canvas layoutsubtree>` via `lib.Html`. `.css-glass` is used for things liquid glass doesn't draw.\n   - **Tooltips:** `TooltipLayer`, using `data-tooltip`; liquid only for anchors in `.capture-bar, .view-dock`.\n   - **Appearance options (`src/lib/appearance.ts`):** stored in localStorage key \"appearance\", via `useAppearance()`.\n   - **Shortcut parsing:** `appKeyboardShortcut` in `src/lib/keyboardShortcuts.ts`.\n   - **Electron verification workflow:**\n     1. `bunx vite build --mode electron-preview`.\n     2. `S=$(mktemp -d); echo $S > /tmp/ink-scratch; mkdir -p $S/ud`.\n     3. Launch with `(unset ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE; node_modules/electron/dist/electron.exe . --preview --user-data-dir=\"$(cygpath -w $S/ud)\" --remote-debugging-port=0 >$S/out.log 2>&1 & echo $! > $S/pid)`.\n     4. Read the port from `$S/ud/DevToolsActivePort` into `$S/port`.\n     5. Bring the window forward with `W=$(cat /proc/$(cat $S/pid)/winpid); powershell -NoProfile -Command \"(New-Object -ComObject WScript.Shell).AppActivate($W)\"`. A hidden window stops rAF and ResizeObserver from running.\n     6. Drive it with `C:/Users/chris/AppData/Local/Temp/agents/liquid-glass-run/drive.ts <port> <shotName|-> '<js body using ev(), click(x,y,button), move(x,y), key(k,code), sleep(ms)>'`. Screenshots go to `C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\sidebar\\`. `reload.ts <port>` reloads the page.\n     7. Cleanup: `kill $(cat $S/pid); rm -rf \"$S\" /tmp/ink-scratch; MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1 reg import \"$(cygpath -w $PWD/inkling-protocol.reg)\"`, run from the liquid-glass-run dir. Electron overwrites the inkling:// handler, and the backup is `inkling-protocol.reg`. Plain `reg export ... /y` fails in Git Bash without `MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1`.\n   - **Checks:** `bunx tsc-rs --noEmit`, `bunx biome check --write <files>`, `bunx knip`, `bun test <file>`.\n   - **Commit:** `timeout 60 git -c core.hooksPath=/nonexistent commit -q -F -` with a heredoc ending \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\", then `git push -q`.\n   - **Editing:**\n     - Python edits use `io.open(..., newline='')` and preserve CRLF/LF.\n     - Backslashes in TS template literals got mangled by shell/python escaping; use the Edit tool for those.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **src/App.css**, desktop `@media (min-width: 781px)` block (the edge grip CSS is the current focus):\n     - Before the media block:\n       ```css\n       /* The narrow layout keeps its buttons; the grip is desktop only. */\n       .edge-grip { display: none; }\n       ```\n     - In the media block:\n       ```css\n       .sidebar.is-open:not(:hover, :focus-within) .sidebar-close { opacity: 0; }\n       .sidebar-edge .sidebar-close, .sidebar-edge .sidebar-toggle { display: none; }\n       .edge-grip { position:absolute; top: calc(4px + var(--titlebar-height)); bottom:20px; left:0; z-index:32; display:block; width:14px; padding:0; border:0; background:none; cursor:pointer; transition: left 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1); }\n       .edge-grip.is-open { left: calc(var(--sidebar-width) - 9px); width: 18px; }\n       .edge-grip:focus-visible { outline: 0; }\n       .edge-grip-bar { position:absolute; top:50%; left:5px; width:4px; height:40px; translate:0 -50%; border-radius:2px; background: var(--library-text); opacity:0.22; transition: opacity .18s ease, height .18s ease; }\n       .edge-grip.is-open .edge-grip-bar { left: 7px; opacity: 0; }\n       .edge-grip-knob { position:absolute; top:50%; left:22px; width:28px; height:28px; display:grid; place-items:center; margin-top:-14px; border-radius:50%; color: var(--library-text); opacity:0; scale:0.85; pointer-events:none; transition: opacity .18s ease, scale .18s ease; }\n       .edge-grip.is-open .edge-grip-knob { left: 25px; }\n       .edge-grip:not(.is-open) .edge-grip-knob svg { rotate: 180deg; }\n       .edge-grip:is(:hover, :focus-visible) .edge-grip-bar { height:56px; opacity:0.6; }\n       .edge-grip:is(:hover, :focus-visible) .edge-grip-knob { opacity:1; scale:1; pointer-events:auto; }\n       ```\n     - `.sidebar-toggle` base rule: glass circle, absolute, `top:50%; left:0; translate:0 -50%`, 34×34, radius 17px. Hover changes color; active uses `scale: 0.96`. The old `left` offsets for `.sidebar-toggle` in the 1120px and 780px media queries were removed.\n     - The `.edge-tab` CSS and its keyframes were removed.\n     - `.library-scroll`: `--library-rest-gap` was removed. `.library-scroll .library-grid { padding-top: var(--scroll-reach-top); padding-bottom: calc(var(--scroll-reach-bottom) + 36px); }`. The column min-height rule was removed. `.has-pinned-query` padding-top is still `calc(var(--scroll-reach-top) + 100px)`.\n     - Item view: `--item-inset: 8px; --item-inspector-top: calc(3px + var(--titlebar-height));`. `.item-stage` uses `inset: var(--item-inset) 320px var(--item-inset) var(--item-inset)`, `border-radius: calc(var(--frame-radius) - 1px - var(--item-inset) + 4px)` and `padding: 60px 40px`.\n   - **src/App.tsx**\n     - `SidebarEdgeGrip({isOpen,onToggle})` sits before `function App()`. It renders `<button className={`edge-grip ${isOpen ? \"is-open\" : \"\"}`} aria-label aria-expanded aria-controls=\"library-navigation\">` containing `<span className=\"edge-grip-bar\" />` and `<span className=\"edge-grip-knob css-glass\" data-tooltip={`${label} · Ctrl+\\\\`}>` with the `ArrowLeft01Icon` icon (size 14, strokeWidth 2).\n     - The grip renders after `</aside>` when `appearance.sidebarToggle === \"edge\" && (isSidebarOpen || !selectedItem)`.\n     - The app-shell className includes `sidebar-edge` when the edge mode is on.\n     - `.sidebar-close`: aria-label \"Close sidebar\", aria-expanded, aria-controls, `data-tooltip=\"Close sidebar\"`. `.sidebar-toggle glass`: aria-label and `data-tooltip` \"Open sidebar\".\n     - Focus handoff effect after the `isSidebarOpen` state uses `sidebarOpenedRef` to skip the first run. It focuses the other button when the active element is the body or `.sidebar-close`/`.sidebar-toggle`.\n     - The card menu is wrapped in `<div ref={cardMenuLayerRef}>`, and `cardMenuLayerRef` was added to the LiquidGlass `targetRoots`.\n     - The global key handler adds `else if (shortcut === \"sidebar\") setIsSidebarOpen((open) => !open);`. The shortcuts sheet gained a row for `Ctrl` or `⌘` + `\\` → \"Show or hide the sidebar\".\n     - Settings → Appearance gained a \"Sidebar button\" row (`SidebarLeftIcon`, a `SegmentedControl` named \"appearance-sidebar-toggle\").\n     - The rest-scroll hold effect and `restScrollKey` were removed.\n   - **src/lib/appearance.ts:** added `sidebarToggle: [{value:\"buttons\",label:\"Buttons\"},{value:\"edge\",label:\"Edge grip\"}]`. `pick` now reads:\n     ```ts\n     const options = APPEARANCE_OPTIONS[key];\n     const option = options.find((candidate) => candidate.value === stored[key]) ?? options[0];\n     // TypeScript cannot tie a generic key's options to that key's values.\n     return option.value as Appearance[Key];\n     ```\n     It returns `{ viewToggle: pick(\"viewToggle\"), sidebarToggle: pick(\"sidebarToggle\") }`.\n   - **src/lib/keyboardShortcuts.ts:** the type adds `\"sidebar\"`. With Ctrl or Meta held: shift returns null, `k` returns `\"search\"`, and `event.key === \"\\\\\"` returns `\"sidebar\"`. The test file has a new test, \"toggles the sidebar with the platform backslash chord\"; 4 tests pass.\n   - **src/components/LiquidGlass.tsx:** a `keepingScroll(content, move)` helper preserves `scrollTop`/`scrollLeft` of every scrolled descendant across `new LiquidSurface(...)` and `wrap.append(content)`.\n   - **src/components/ContextMenu/ContextMenu.tsx and .css:** no portal; it renders inline with className `context-menu glass`. The CSS dropped its own border, background and shadow.\n   - **docs/changelog.md (#170 entries):**\n     - Appearance line now covers both the view toggle and the sidebar button.\n     - New Ctrl+\\ line.\n     - \"The sidebar closes from a button beside the inkling wordmark… replacing the tab\" (Changed).\n     - The library first-row line (Fixed).\n     - The right-click menu line mentions glass.\n     - The item-view line no longer mentions the tab.\n   - **Mockup:** `C:/Users/chris/AppData/Local/Temp/agents/mock-d/d.html`, the D hi-fi mockup, already rendered.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Close flight stuck in `is-flying`:** the scratch window was occluded, so rAF never fired. Fixed with `Page.bringToFront` and AppActivate; it was not an app bug.\n   - **Rest scroll failed at cold launch:** the root cause was liquid glass moving the content into its canvas, which reset `scrollTop`. Fixed with `keepingScroll`. The rest gap was later removed entirely at the user's request.\n   - **Focus handoff didn't trigger:** the clicked close button stays focused during the 0.3s visibility transition. Fixed by also matching `.sidebar-close`/`.sidebar-toggle` as the active element.\n   - **Template literal `Ctrl+\\`` broke parsing:** shell and python escaping kept dropping a backslash. Fixed with the Edit tool to `Ctrl+\\\\`.\n   - **TS error in `pick`:** generic indexing. Fixed with an `as Appearance[Key]` cast and a comment.\n   - **`.edge-grip` stayed `display:none` on desktop:** the base rule hid it. Fixed by adding `display:block` in the media rule.\n   - **`reg export ... /y` failed:** Git Bash path conversion. Fixed with `MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1`. Restores used the existing `inkling-protocol.reg`.\n   - **Stray comment line in `ExpandedItemOverlay`:** fixed in follow-up commit `5520c2f`.\n   - **Python `.format`/escape SyntaxWarnings:** harmless.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Verified in Electron:**\n     - Cold-launch first card at y=37.\n     - Scrolling up can't pull the library down, in grid and list.\n     - Header close button and glass toggle, with focus handoff.\n     - Liquid-glass context menu.\n     - Edge grip in both states, with hover knob and tooltip \"Open sidebar · Ctrl+\\\".\n     - Ctrl+\\ toggles both ways.\n     - Settings switches modes live.\n   - **Limitation:** the tooltip shows only when the pointer is on the knob, and it sits below it. The knob uses CSS glass.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"[screenshot] also get rid of the sidebar close button when the sidebar is closed and the item details are open and then adjust the the item viewer so that it makes uses of this whitespace in a sensible and good looking way\"\n   - \"what other ways can we style the sidebar close button? i honestly dont like the way we have it\"\n   - \"[screenshot] yeah do C and put the library by default at this height and make the sidebar close button liquid glass when its on top of the library … but also mockup d at a higher fidelity because I might want that one\"\n   - \"also the right click menu got left out with liquid glass so fix that\"\n   - \"add it as another toggle in settings and include D as well so I can compare them later\"\n   - \"[screenshot] the library can still scroll down more, i dont want that\"\n   - \"when the sidebar is opened that should ever so slightly be over to the right, in the library side [screenshot of edge grip hovered, sidebar open, with a mark just right of the grip bar]\"\n   - Standing instructions: \"commit and push to 170 when your done just not to 174 yet\". AGENTS.md rules also apply:\n     - Never kill processes by name or pattern; only the captured PID.\n     - Never write to the live library.\n     - No hardcoded ports or paths.\n     - No PRs unless asked.\n     - No repo-wide checks.\n     - Test UI in the real app, with screenshots in `chat-images`.\n     - Changelog: one line per entry.\n     - Don't commit scratch files.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Nudge the edge grip slightly right, into the library frame, when the sidebar is open: the bar, and likely the knob.\n   - Verify in Electron with a screenshot, update the changelog only if warranted (probably no new line; it's a tweak), then commit and push to #170.\n   - Later, when the user picks C or D, delete the other and the setting. Not requested yet.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   The user's latest message, about Edge grip mode with the sidebar open, reads: \"when the sidebar is opened that should ever so slightly be over to the right, in the library side\". The current open-state CSS is:\n   ```css\n   .edge-grip.is-open { left: calc(var(--sidebar-width) - 9px); width: 18px; }\n   .edge-grip.is-open .edge-grip-bar { left: 7px; opacity: 0; }\n   .edge-grip.is-open .edge-grip-knob { left: 25px; }\n   ```\n   With these values the bar straddles the frame border at x≈`sidebar-width`. It should sit a few pixels inside the library frame.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   In `src/App.css`, move the open-state grip bar a few px right so it sits just inside the library frame. For example, set `.edge-grip.is-open .edge-grip-bar { left: 13px; }`, which puts the bar about 4px inside the border, and nudge `.edge-grip.is-open .edge-grip-knob` to about `left: 29px`. Then:\n   1. Rebuild and launch the scratch Electron with Edge grip mode (`localStorage.setItem(\"appearance\", JSON.stringify({viewToggle:\"pill\", sidebarToggle:\"edge\"}))`, then reload).\n   2. Hover at (sidebar edge + ~6, 360) and screenshot.\n   3. Run biome on `App.css`.\n   4. Clean up (kill PID, reg import, rm scratch).\n   5. Commit and push to #170.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\chris\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"a6f84446-3c5e-495e-bdf4-6a56c03a081b","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:56:37.869Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":0,"turnIndex":179},"turnOrigin":"sdk","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["636dbbe4-acbf-44cc-a4c2-ca8dda8d7410"],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
