{"parentUuid":"1d96c940-a75c-46f1-beff-57770e1e398a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGHi3duTuRcp8FBuZrXd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm checking whether there's any UI for creating smart spaces with a favorite filter, and it seems the creation flow never sets favorite, so it's only used via the seed. I'm deciding to strip favorite out of the frontend entirely—types, seed data, smart queries, pin toggle, overlay star, and card menu.\n\nFor the backend, I need to check whether removing favorite from the query validation would break any existing stored smart space that had that filter, since stale data could trigger a rejection. Given pins are user data worth protecting, I'm leaning toward leaving the DB column in place as a dormant, unused field rather than risk breaking saved pins, and I'll note that tradeoff. Let me look at the storage code around those relevant line ranges.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3318,"cache_read_input_tokens":71613,"output_tokens":653,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":480},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3318,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":653,"cache_read_input_tokens":71613,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3318,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3318},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7556,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGHi3HKbaJVjZ4K3XCuC","requestRef":"fd639d19-564e-49ae-82eb-fff431b93c87","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assis